{"id":"sw-3afd48","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5368e5c4-cdea-4078-9ee1-edda38f41da2","text":"## Summary\n\nBrick pool allocator in `crates/engine/src/brick_pool.rs`.\n\n**`BrickHandle`** — `{ slot: u32, generation: u32 }` with `gpu_index()` for buffer addressing and `NONE` sentinel for empty index entries.\n\n**`BrickPool`** — owns two GPU storage buffers:\n- `voxel_buf`: `capacity × 4 KB` (16³ × u8, packed 4-per-u32 = 1024 words/brick)\n- `palette_buf`: `capacity × 1 KB` (256 × RGBA32 packed as u32)\n\nFree-list stack for O(1) alloc/free. Per-slot generation counter detects stale handles (debug_assert on free, `is_valid()` for queries). `write_voxels` packs 4096 bytes into 1024 u32s and uploads to the correct buffer offset. `write_palette` packs RGBA entries as u32.\n\n**Also modified:** `crates/engine/Cargo.toml` (added `pollster` as dev-dependency for tests), `crates/engine/src/lib.rs` (registered module).\n\n## Rationale\n\nTwo separate buffers (voxels + palettes) rather than one interleaved buffer. The raymarcher's hot path accesses voxels only; palettes are touched once per hit. Separating them avoids polluting the cache with palette data during traversal.\n\n## Decisions made\n\nNone beyond the spec.\n\n## Status\n\n`cargo clippy` and `cargo test` (21 tests, 7 new) pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T23:06:35.422659Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
