{"id":"sw-15accc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-72c6903f-2814-4803-9b49-1c8e0e24c808","text":"## Summary\n\nSun shadow ray and optional smooth normals, both toggleable from the debug panel.\n\n**Shader changes** (`raymarch.wgsl`):\n- Restructured `trace_brick` to return unshaded hit info (`base_color`, `normal`, `voxel`, `handle`, `world_pos`)\n- `trace_shadow(ro, rd) -\u003e bool` — stripped-down two-level DDA, no color/normal/palette, early-exits on first solid hit\n- `smooth_normal(handle, voxel, face_normal) -\u003e vec3` — 6-neighbor central differences of occupancy, out-of-brick treated as air\n- Shading moved to main loop: normal selection → NdotL → shadow ray → final color\n- Uniform `_pad1` repurposed as `flags` (bit 0 = shadows, bit 1 = smooth normals)\n\n**Rust changes:**\n- `Raymarcher::render()` accepts `flags: u32`; constants `FLAG_SHADOWS` and `FLAG_SMOOTH_NORMALS`\n- Viewer: `shadows: bool` (default true), `smooth_normals: bool` (default false) in `RunState`, checkboxes in debug panel\n\n## Status\n\nTests pass, clippy clean. Shadow ray confirmed working — sphere casts shadow on ground. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-05T23:51:47.664619Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
