{"id":"sw-5d894d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b9b61c82-60b7-41ff-b63f-db9442df7149","text":"## Summary\n\nVoxel object types and scene infrastructure for instanced rendering.\n\n**New files:**\n- `crates/engine/src/voxel_object.rs` — `VoxelModel` (local brick grid + voxel scale), `VoxelInstance` (model ref + position + rotation), `VoxelInstanceGpu` (160-byte packed struct for shader)\n- `crates/engine/src/scene.rs` — `Scene` holding models + instances with packed GPU buffers (grid buffer + instance buffer)\n- `crates/engine/src/model_gen.rs` — procedural tree (2.5cm, ~5-voxel trunk, ellipsoidal canopy) and rock (2.5cm, varied ellipsoid) generators\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `crates/engine/src/worldgen.rs` — exposed `approx_surface_y`, added `hash_for_placement`\n- `crates/engine/src/lib.rs` — registered 3 new modules\n- `crates/viewer/src/main.rs` — creates `Scene`, populates with 27 trees + 12 rocks scattered on terrain, debug panel shows instance count, pool increased to 32768\n\n## Status\n\n25 tests pass, clippy clean. Scene populates: 39 instances, 2 models (tree + rock at 2.5cm), 1502 packed grid cells. Objects invisible until sw-06bbbc (traversal). Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T00:54:32.493458Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
