{"id":"sw-70506a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Procedural tree generator v2: recursive branching with leaf volumes","description":"Replace the current trunk+ellipsoid tree model with a recursive branching structure: main trunk tapers upward, large branches fork off at varied angles, each branch subdivides 2-3 times into smaller branches, and ellipsoidal leaf volumes cap each terminal branch. L-system or space colonization algorithm. At 2.5cm voxel scale, trunks should be 4-8 voxels wide at the base, branches 2-3 voxels, producing visually convincing trees.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"ap","labels":["feature","worldgen"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T01:11:02.472944Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-06bbbc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-49a6e5f2-72a3-41c0-96d3-59c30fccf228","text":"## Summary\n\nTwo-level ray traversal: rays test terrain first, then linear-scan all object instances. Each object ray is transformed into object space and runs the same grid+brick DDA with per-instance voxel scale.\n\n**Shader** (`raymarch.wgsl`): Major rewrite — refactored terrain traversal into `trace_terrain()`, added `trace_object()` for per-instance traversal (inv_transform ray, local grid DDA, world-space hit conversion), shadow ray extended to test objects. Main loop finds closest hit across terrain + all instances.\n\n**Raymarcher** (`raymarcher.rs`): 7-binding compute layout (added instance + object grid buffers). Dummy buffers for empty scene. Uniform extended with `instance_count`.\n\n**Worldgen**: Removed baked 10cm terrain trees. Added `find_surface_y()` for accurate object placement via density zero-crossing search.\n\n## Status\n\n25 tests pass, clippy clean. 2.5cm trees and rocks render on 10cm terrain with correct occlusion and shadows."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T01:11:28.742788Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
