{"id":"sw-e5b644","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:42:29.56291Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"sw-2c3e44","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Job System\n\nEngine-managed thread pool for offloading work from the main/render thread.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Worker pool** — fixed thread count (cores - 2 or configurable), work-stealing\n- **Priority scheduling** — urgent (physics, audio feed) vs. normal (AI ticks, worldgen) vs. background (compaction, saves)\n- **Cancellation** — cooperative cancel tokens for long-running jobs\n- **Dependency graph** — job A depends on job B; automatic ordering\n- **Main-thread callbacks** — results posted back to main thread via channel\n\n### Non-goals (game crate territory)\n\n- Specific AI behaviors\n- Worldgen job orchestration\n- Save-game serialization jobs\n\n### Technical direction\n\nLock-free job queue per priority level. Each worker pops from highest non-empty queue. Likely uses `std::thread` + crossbeam channels rather than async runtime — predictable latency matters more than throughput.","estimate":8,"labels":["epic","engine","infra"],"sort_order":"aq","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Job System: background worker pool, scheduling"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:52:50.429221Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e5dcab","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Save/Load Infrastructure\n\nEngine-level serialization framework for persisting and restoring world state.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **World serialization format** — binary format for brick data, palette, index, scene graph\n- **Incremental saves** — dirty-region tracking, only write modified chunks/bricks\n- **Asset packaging** — bundle models, palettes, scripts into loadable archives\n- **Version migration** — format versioning with forward-compatible reader\n\n### Non-goals (game crate territory)\n\n- Save game slots and UI\n- Player state serialization\n- Game-specific metadata (quest progress, inventory)\n\n### Technical direction\n\nRegion-file approach (like Minecraft's .mca): each world region is a separate file, header + compressed brick data. Dirty flag per region, written on save. Engine provides read/write primitives; game decides when and what to save.","estimate":8,"labels":["epic","engine","persistence"],"sort_order":"ar","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Save/Load Infrastructure: serialization, dirty-region tracking"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:53:04.146022Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ee6306","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Audio Engine\n\nThe engine provides a low-level audio toolkit that games build on top of.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Multi-channel mixer** — play N sounds simultaneously, per-channel gain (dB), pan\n- **Ducking** — automatic gain reduction on lower-priority channels when high-priority plays (e.g. dialogue ducks music)\n- **Cross-fading** — smooth transitions between tracks (music, ambience)\n- **Spatial audio** — 3D positioned sources with distance attenuation, HRTF or simple panning\n- **Effects bus** — reverb, low-pass, echo; routable per-channel or global\n- **Format support** — WAV/OGG at minimum, streaming for long tracks\n\n### Non-goals (game crate territory)\n\n- Specific sound assets\n- Music playlists / jukebox logic\n- Dialogue systems\n\n### Technical direction\n\nLikely wraps `cpal` for output device, custom lock-free mixer on a dedicated audio thread. Ring buffer for command submission from game thread.","labels":["epic","engine","audio"],"sort_order":"as","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Audio Engine: multi-channel mixer, spatial audio, effects"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:53:31.138654Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-daeb58","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## UI Framework\n\nEngine-level UI toolkit for building game menus, HUDs, and overlays.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Layout engine** — panels, flex/grid layout, anchoring, scrolling\n- **Primitives** — button, checkbox, dropdown, slider, text input, label, image\n- **Theming/skinning** — style sheets or theme objects for colors, fonts, spacing\n- **Input routing** — mouse/keyboard/gamepad focus, tab order, modal stacking\n- **Render integration** — either extends egui or replaces it with a voxel-styled UI rendered through wgpu\n\n### Non-goals (game crate territory)\n\n- Specific menu screens (main menu, inventory, pause)\n- HUD layout and content\n- Game-specific widget compositions\n\n### Open questions\n\n- Build on egui (mature, immediate mode) vs. custom retained-mode UI?\n- Voxel-styled rendering (pixel art fonts, blocky frames) vs. clean vector UI?","labels":["epic","engine","ui"],"sort_order":"at","status":"BACKLOG","title":"UI Framework: layout engine, primitives, theming"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:53:38.349288Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-8a89c4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Scripting Runtime\n\nEmbedded scripting language for game rules, AI behaviors, and mod support.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Language runtime** — Rhai (pure Rust, safe) or Lua via mlua (fast, ecosystem)\n- **Engine API bindings** — spawn/despawn entities, query voxels, edit bricks, play sounds, show UI, read input\n- **Script execution** — scripts run in job system workers, sandboxed, with per-frame budget (instruction count limit)\n- **Hot reload** — watch script files, reload on change without restart\n- **Event hooks** — on_tick, on_collide, on_interact, on_damage, etc.\n\n### Non-goals (game crate territory)\n\n- Specific game scripts (monster AI, crafting rules, quest logic)\n- Script asset organization and loading order\n\n### Open questions\n\n- Rhai vs. Lua? Rhai is safer and pure-Rust but slower and less known. Lua has massive gamedev ecosystem.\n- Entity system: do we need a full ECS (bevy_ecs standalone?) or is the existing VoxelModel/VoxelInstance enough?","labels":["epic","engine","scripting"],"sort_order":"au","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Scripting Runtime: embedded language, engine API bindings"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:53:45.454115Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ef7223","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Game Crate (`crates/game`)\n\nA specific game built on the smallworld engine. The engine is a toolkit; this crate is the product.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Crate scaffold** — binary crate depending on `smallworld-engine`, wires up app loop, resource loading\n- **Biomes \u0026 palettes** — per-biome palette sets, worldgen parameter tables, biome blending/transitions\n- **Creatures \u0026 AI** — monster model generators, AI behavior scripts, spawn rules, aggro/patrol\n- **Props \u0026 items** — torches (emissive), weapons, furniture, item definitions, loot tables\n- **Menus \u0026 HUD** — main menu, pause screen, inventory, settings — built from engine UI primitives\n- **Save/load game state** — save slots, player state, world persistence — using engine save/load infra\n- **Game rules \u0026 scripts** — progression, crafting, combat rules — script collections running in job workers\n\n### Separation principle\n\nThe engine provides **verbs** (play sound, render voxels, run script, show panel, save region).\nThe game provides **nouns and rules** (this torch, that monster, craft sword from iron + wood).\n\n### Dependencies\n\nThis epic depends on engine infrastructure being available:\n- Audio Engine (for sound)\n- UI Framework (for menus)\n- Job System (for AI workers)\n- Scripting Runtime (for game rules)\n- Save/Load Infrastructure (for persistence)\n- Lighting \u0026 GI (for emissive materials)\n\nContent can be prototyped before all engine systems land by hardcoding where scripts/UI would eventually go.","labels":["epic","game"],"sort_order":"av","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Game Crate: content, rules, and resources for the smallworld game"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:53:48.793028Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b87ab1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Core mixer on a dedicated audio thread. Lock-free command ring from game thread. Per-channel gain (dB), stereo pan, play/pause/stop. Wraps `cpal` for device output.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","audio"],"parent_id":"sw-ee6306","sort_order":"aw","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Multi-channel mixer: play/stop/volume/pan per channel"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:53:59.137897Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-6363ba","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Priority-based ducking (high-priority channel reduces gain on lower channels). Smooth cross-fade between tracks on the same channel group (music, ambience).","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","audio"],"parent_id":"sw-ee6306","sort_order":"ax","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Ducking \u0026 cross-fading between audio channels"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:02.009062Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-34fd9c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"3D sound sources with position relative to listener. Distance attenuation (inverse square or configurable curve). Simple stereo panning from angle; optional HRTF for headphone mode.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","audio"],"parent_id":"sw-ee6306","sort_order":"ay","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Spatial audio: 3D positioned sources, distance attenuation"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:04.141335Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ec9158","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Routable effects pipeline. Each channel can send to one or more effect buses. Built-in effects: reverb (convolution or algorithmic), low-pass filter, echo/delay. Runs on audio thread.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","audio"],"parent_id":"sw-ee6306","sort_order":"az","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Audio effects bus: reverb, low-pass, echo"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:07.079301Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-1bdc98","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Core layout system. Panels with flex/grid children, anchor-based positioning (center, top-left, etc.), overflow scrolling. Resolution-independent (relative units). Builds on or replaces current egui integration.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","ui"],"parent_id":"sw-daeb58","sort_order":"b00","status":"BACKLOG","title":"UI layout engine: panels, flex, anchoring, scrolling"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:09.775405Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-0fb0be","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Standard widget set built on the layout engine. Button (press/hover/disabled states), checkbox, dropdown/select, slider (float/int range), text input (single-line, multi-line), label, image/icon. Keyboard and gamepad navigable.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","ui"],"parent_id":"sw-daeb58","sort_order":"b01","status":"BACKLOG","title":"UI primitives: button, checkbox, dropdown, slider, text input"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:13.066489Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-5f8078","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Theme system for consistent visual styling. Theme object defines colors, font sizes, spacing, border radii. Widgets inherit from current theme. Support for multiple themes (e.g. dark/light, voxel-styled).","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","ui"],"parent_id":"sw-daeb58","sort_order":"b02","status":"BACKLOG","title":"UI theming: style objects, colors, fonts, spacing"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:14.821741Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e475fe","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Fixed-size thread pool (cores - 2 default). Three priority levels: urgent (physics, audio feed), normal (AI, worldgen), background (compaction, saves). Work-stealing between workers. Lock-free job queues per priority. Cooperative cancellation via tokens.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","infra"],"parent_id":"sw-2c3e44","sort_order":"b03","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Worker pool with priority queues and work-stealing"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:19.048859Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ac1601","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Job A can declare dependency on job B — scheduler ensures ordering. Results posted back to main thread via bounded channel. Completion handles for polling or blocking on job groups.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","infra"],"parent_id":"sw-2c3e44","sort_order":"b04","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Job dependency graph and main-thread result callbacks"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:21.140023Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3d9d06","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Embed a scripting language (Rhai or Lua). Sandboxed execution with instruction-count budgets per frame. Scripts run in job system workers. Hot-reload: watch script directory, reload on file change.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","scripting"],"parent_id":"sw-8a89c4","sort_order":"b05","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Script runtime integration: Rhai or Lua, sandboxed execution"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:28.336444Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-95aed3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Script-callable API surface: spawn/despawn entities, query/edit voxels, play sounds, show UI elements, read input state. Event hooks: on_tick, on_collide, on_interact, on_damage. Type-safe wrappers that bridge script values to Rust types.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","scripting"],"parent_id":"sw-8a89c4","sort_order":"b06","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Engine API bindings for scripts: voxels, audio, UI, entities"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:29.058635Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-f5eee5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Binary region-file format: header + compressed brick data per world region. Version tag for forward-compatible reading. Serializes brick pool data, palettes, index, and scene graph. Dirty-region tracking for incremental saves.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","persistence"],"parent_id":"sw-e5dcab","sort_order":"b07","status":"BACKLOG","title":"World serialization format with region files"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:30.723255Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-43d62b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Pack game assets (voxel models, palette files, scripts, sounds) into a single archive. Fast random-access reads via table-of-contents header. Compression optional per entry. Used for distribution and mod packaging.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","persistence"],"parent_id":"sw-e5dcab","sort_order":"b08","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Asset packaging: bundle models, palettes, scripts into archives"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T06:54:33.179313Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
