{"id":"sw-73f01a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a33caf5b-e1ac-4cbf-b767-46d78852cf7f","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a scene preset system with six switchable presets via an egui dropdown.\n\n**New file:** `crates/sandbox/src/scenes.rs` — `Preset` enum with `Default`, `TerrainOnly`, `ObjectsOnly`, `Stress`, `SingleBrick`, `Empty` variants. Each provides grid dims, world bounds, pool capacity, camera start, and a `setup()` function.\n\n**Modified:** `crates/sandbox/src/main.rs`\n- Added `current_preset: Preset` to `RunState`\n- Added `RunState::load_preset()` — rebuilds BrickPool, BrickIndex, Scene, and Raymarcher for the selected preset\n- Wired egui `ComboBox` into the debug panel for runtime switching\n- Removed old inline `generate_world()` / `populate_scene()` (moved into `scenes.rs`)\n- `resumed()` now delegates to `Preset::Default.setup()`\n\n**Rationale:** Isolated test scenes avoid recompilation and allow targeted profiling/debugging of individual engine systems.\n\n**Decisions made:**\n- `_device` parameter kept in `setup()` signature (unused now, but the API contract is right for presets that create GPU resources)\n- Stress preset places 484 instances in a grid (22×22 at 2m spacing) — enough to exercise BVH without exhausting the pool\n- SingleBrick uses a 4-material debug palette (red interior, green face, blue edge, yellow corner) to validate normal/material rendering\n\n**Status:** fmt, clippy, 29 tests, and smoke all pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T07:23:11.581226Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
