{"id":"sw-638630","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2690bd6e-acf2-4efe-bbcf-45d536954c8f","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded 4-level intra-brick mip chain (8³, 4³, 2³, 1³) with pre-averaged RGBA per mip voxel.\n\n**New file:** `crates/engine/src/mip.rs` — `compute_brick_mips()` builds all 4 levels from voxel data + palette. 585 u32 words per brick. RGB averages non-air children, alpha = occupancy fraction. 3 unit tests.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `crates/engine/src/brick_pool.rs` — added `mip_buf`, `write_mips()`, `mip_buffer()` accessor\n- `crates/engine/src/voxel_object.rs` — `fill_brick()` computes and uploads mips alongside voxels/palette\n- `crates/engine/src/raymarcher.rs` — binding 8 for mip buffer in layout + bind group + resize\n- `crates/engine/shaders/common.wgsl` — `MIP_WORDS_PER_BRICK` constant\n- `crates/engine/shaders/raymarch.wgsl` — `sample_brick_mip()` replaces `sample_brick_lod()`, graduated LOD selection via `log2(threshold/sse)`, spatially-aware lookup keyed by ray entry point. Also renamed `trace_terrain` → `trace_grid`, `trace_object` → `trace_instance`.\n- `crates/sandbox/src/scenes.rs` — terrain and single-brick presets compute and upload mips\n\n**Rationale:** Properly filtered average colors make LOD transitions seamless — the coarse representation visually matches fine detail. The probe-based hack produced color mismatches.\n\n**Known limitation:** At SSE \u003e 0.8, brick boundaries become visible as a grid pattern because each brick averages independently. Cross-brick mip blending would fix this but requires neighbor handle lookups. Default threshold set to 0.8.\n\n**Status:** fmt, clippy, 32 tests, smoke pass. Mip transitions visually confirmed smooth."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:03:54.035449Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
