{"id":"sw-9debe6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Allow games to register custom compute/render passes alongside the engine's built-in raymarcher. The asset override system (`assets.rs`) already supports runtime shader loading — this story adds the API for games to register additional passes, override the built-in shaders, or inject post-processing stages.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine"],"sort_order":"b0O","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Custom shader pass registration API for games"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:07:11.20222Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-9debe6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"parent_id":"sw-ef7223","sort_order":"b08"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:07:47.420187Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"sw-a6a691","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a6a691","target_id":"sw-638630"}],"description":"When the SSE fallback shades from mip data, adjacent bricks with different average colors create a visible grid pattern at distance. Fix by reading neighbor brick mip values in the shader and interpolating at brick boundaries.\n\nRequires:\n- Neighbor handle lookup in the shader (the grid_map already contains handles for all grid positions — index arithmetic gives the 6-neighbor handles)\n- Trilinear interpolation of mip colors near brick edges\n- Fallback when a neighbor slot is EMPTY (use the current brick's color)\n\nThis is the proper fix for the per-brick mip seam artifact visible at SSE \u003e 0.8. Distance fog (Atmosphere epic) and larger worlds (Streaming) reduce visibility but don't eliminate the root cause.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","rendering","perf"],"parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","sort_order":"aq","status":"PLANNED","title":"Cross-brick mip blending at grid boundaries"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:09:08.960662Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
