{"id":"sw-943a75","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2de97857-8480-4716-aa1e-db88adb7174d","text":"\n## Summary\n\nImplemented async brick paging with residency tracking, LRU eviction, and disk-backed region caching.\n\n**Engine** (3 new modules):\n- `brick_data.rs` — `BrickData` struct shared between sources and pager\n- `brick_source.rs` — `BrickSource` trait for game-provided brick data\n- `brick_pager.rs` — `BrickPager` orchestrator: demand computation from camera SSE, `crossbeam-channel` worker threads, per-cell state machine (Unknown→Loading→Resident→MipOnly→Air), LRU eviction, per-frame upload cap (64/frame)\n- `BrickPool::reassign()` and `BrickIndex::clear_cell()` added\n\n**Sandbox** (2 new modules):\n- `region.rs` — `.swr` region file format (16³ cells/file, sector-based, zstd-compressed)\n- `cached_source.rs` — `CachedSource\u003cS\u003e` wrapper: disk-first, generate-on-miss, write-back\n\n**Integration**: Default and TerrainOnly presets use paged loading. Debug panel shows pager stats. Bench mode works with streaming.\n\n## Rationale\n\nEngine provides the primitives (`BrickSource`, `BrickPager`); persistence (region files, `CachedSource`) is sandbox/game code. This keeps the engine agnostic about where brick data comes from.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- **Air state** added to cell state machine (not in original spec) — prevents infinite re-request loops for confirmed-empty cells\n- **Bench preset parser** fixed to handle hyphens (\"terrain-only\" → \"TerrainOnly\")\n- `bytemuck` added to sandbox deps (needed for region file header I/O)\n- Region files written to `~/.cache/smallworld/sandbox/{preset}/regions/`\n\n## Status\n\nAll 34 tests passing, clippy clean, fmt clean. Benchmark verified: 7630 bricks stream in via pager, second launch hits region cache (no worldgen log).\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:40:44.727205Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-943a75","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"walkthrough","filename":"walkthrough.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:41:32.660267Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ed6340","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-ed6340","target_id":"sw-943a75"}],"description":"\nMove terrain noise evaluation from CPU threads to a GPU compute shader. Currently each brick requires ~12K noise evaluations (~1ms/brick on CPU). At scale (128×16×128 = 262K cells), CPU procgen takes 4+ minutes — unusable for testing the paging system.\n\n**Approach:**\n- Compute shader implementing the same fbm3d noise + density/material logic as `worldgen.rs`\n- Dispatch in batches (e.g. 256 bricks per dispatch), each workgroup fills one brick's voxel data\n- Read back via buffer mapping → feed into pager as `BrickData`\n- The `BrickSource` trait stays for CPU sources; the pager gets a parallel GPU-accelerated generation path\n\n**Why GPU:** The noise math is embarrassingly parallel — 4096 independent voxels per brick, each doing the same fbm3d evaluation. This is exactly what GPU compute excels at. Expected speedup: 100-1000× over CPU threads.\n\n**Enables:** Large-world sandbox presets that actually exercise the paging/eviction/streaming system at scale.\n","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","perf"],"parent_id":"sw-d6d2c2","sort_order":"ar","status":"PLANNED","title":"GPU compute noise generation for brick data"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T10:04:22.312574Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
