{"id":"sw-ff3ae3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"\nReplace the flat brick grid (BrickIndex + grid DDA) with a Sparse Voxel Octree that provides seamless, continuous LOD by construction. Target: 1 km × 1 km world, 10 cm terrain voxels, 1-2.5 cm object voxels, 30-60 fps on M1 Max, zero LOD pop.\n\n**Why SVO:** A ray descends the tree and stops at the node level where it's sub-pixel. Each interior node stores the average color of its children. There are no brick boundaries, no LOD transitions, no seams — the tree IS the LOD hierarchy. This is what GigaVoxels, SVDAG, and Atomontage all use.\n\n**What survives from current engine:** BrickPool (leaf brick storage), GPU worldgen (noise evaluation), streaming pager (adapted for subtrees), region cache, adapter limit fix.\n\n**What gets replaced:** BrickIndex (flat grid → octree), grid DDA in shader (→ octree descent).\n","labels":["epic","rendering","perf"],"sort_order":"b0T","title":"SVO rendering: seamless LOD for km-scale voxel worlds"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T13:06:51.705815Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
