{"id":"sw-a708d5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"SVO node structure + GPU buffer layout","description":"\nDefine the octree node format and flat-array GPU representation. Each interior node: 8 child pointers (indices into the node array) + averaged RGBA color + valid-children bitmask. Leaf nodes: brick handle into the existing BrickPool. The tree replaces BrickIndex.\n\nTree depth for 1 km at 10 cm: log2(10000) ≈ 14 levels. Node count for terrain: ~20-50M nodes (sparse — most is air). At 32-48 bytes/node: 1-2 GB. Fits in M1 Max 4 GB buffer limit.\n","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-ff3ae3","estimate":3,"sort_order":"b0U","labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T13:07:16.313848Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-f089de","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"SVO construction from GPU noise + streaming","description":"\nBuild the octree from the terrain density function. Two modes:\n\n1. **Top-down coarse pass** — evaluate noise at each octree level's resolution to determine occupancy. Start from root, subdivide only where density crosses the surface. This builds the full tree structure in seconds for a 1 km world.\n\n2. **Bottom-up leaf refinement** — near the camera, generate full 16³ brick data (existing GPU worldgen) and attach as leaf nodes. The existing pager streams leaf bricks on demand.\n\nAdapt the pager to load/evict SVO subtrees instead of flat grid cells.\n","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-ff3ae3","estimate":5,"sort_order":"b0V","labels":["feature","engine","sandbox"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T13:07:28.530863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"1 km world validation: terrain + objects at target spec","description":"\nThe proof-of-concept preset that validates the full target:\n- 1 km × 1 km terrain at 10 cm voxels\n- Instanced objects at 1-2.5 cm voxels\n- Seamless rendering — no LOD pop, no seams, no discontinuities\n- 30-60 fps on M1 Max\n- Benchmark harness to verify all criteria\n","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-ff3ae3","estimate":3,"sort_order":"b0W","labels":["feature","sandbox"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T13:07:31.37441Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-bd0852","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"SVO raymarcher: octree descent replacing grid DDA","description":"\nCompute shader that traces rays through the octree instead of the flat grid. Uses a stack-based descent: push root, test AABB, if hit descend to children. SSE at each node determines whether to shade from the node's averaged color (distant) or descend further (nearby). At leaf nodes with brick handles, call existing trace_brick for fine DDA.\n\nSeamless LOD is automatic — the ray stops at the tree level where the node is sub-pixel. The averaged color at each level IS the correct LOD representation. No transitions, no boundaries.\n","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-ff3ae3","estimate":5,"sort_order":"b0X","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-bd0852","target_id":"sw-a708d5","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T13:07:42.149174Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
