{"id":"sw-1293d8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"trace_brick returns brick entry t instead of voxel hit t","description":"Found while debugging grid-shaped chasms under sw-bd0852.\n\n`trace_brick` in `raymarch.wgsl` returns `t_enter` (the t at which the ray enters the brick AABB) as the hit `t`, regardless of which voxel inside the brick was actually hit.\n\n**Consequences:**\n\n- `trace_svo` uses `best.t` for front-to-back culling (`t_near \u003e= best.t` skips nodes). A brick whose surface lies deep inside (e.g. terrain surface below the cell top) records an artificially early `t`, culling neighboring nodes whose true surface is closer — missing/incorrect geometry near brick silhouettes.\n- Brick-vs-instance ordering in `cs_main` compares the brick's entry t against instance hit t — object instances (trees, rocks) can be wrongly occluded by terrain that is actually behind them.\n\n**Fix:** track the DDA crossing t (`t_local` = the `t_max` component chosen at each step, before increment) and return `t_enter + bias + t_local` as the hit t.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"b0Y","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-1293d8","target_id":"sw-bd0852","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T15:16:43.324787Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-fcea39","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pager eviction leaves stale brick handle in SVO leaf","description":"Found while debugging grid-shaped chasms under sw-bd0852. Filed for the pager adaptation in sw-f089de — not fixed now because eviction never triggers in current presets (pool capacity 32768 \u003e 7630 resident bricks).\n\nIn `brick_pager.rs::drain_results`, when the pool is exhausted the pager evicts an LRU slot via `pool.reassign(old_slot)` and hands the slot to a new cell. The comment says \"SVO eviction: the node stays with its averaged color for LOD\" — but the evicted cell's SVO leaf still has flag bit 8 (`has brick`) set and `brick = old_slot`. The raymarcher will read the slot's **new** contents at the **old** cell's location, rendering the wrong brick there instead of falling back to the averaged color.\n\n**Fix (in sw-f089de):** add `Svo::remove_brick(world_pos, leaf_size)` (or equivalent) that clears flag bit 8 and the handle on eviction, leaving the averaged color for LOD fallback.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"b0X","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-fcea39","target_id":"sw-bd0852","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"sw-fcea39","target_id":"sw-f089de","kind":"dependency_of"}],"labels":["bug","engine"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T15:16:49.532279Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
