{"id":"sw-bd0852","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T15:19:33.852126Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-bd0852","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-cef2856a-1e74-4f2f-90da-910a7ea65261","text":"## Chasm fix round\n\n**Summary** — Grid-shaped chasms were caused by f32 octant misclassification in `Svo::insert_brick`: brick min corners sit exactly on octree split planes, and the `pos \u003e= center` test compared two different f32 rounding paths (accumulated halving vs `world_min + g * BRICK_SIZE`). Bricks at x/z indices 7, 14, 15, 19, 20, 23, 25, 28, 30 and y 5, 7 landed one cell low — overwriting their neighbor's leaf and leaving their own cell empty. Adjacent bad indices (14+15, 19+20) produced the two-brick-wide canyons.\n\n**Fix** — `insert_brick` now snaps the position to integer leaf coordinates once (f64, `round()`) and descends by bit tests — no float comparisons in the descent, exact at any depth. Numeric proof of the misclassification is attached as `chasm-fp-analysis.md`.\n\n**Also fixed** — `trace_brick` returned the brick entry t instead of the true voxel hit t, corrupting front-to-back culling and terrain-vs-object ordering (filed and fixed as sw-1293d8). Eviction stale-handle gap in the pager filed as sw-fcea39 for sw-f089de — inert in current presets.\n\n**Decisions made** — kept the `insert_brick(world_pos, ...)` signature (callers unchanged) but documented that `world_pos` is the leaf's min corner, snapped to the lattice. Chose exact integer descent over inserting at brick centers: centers would merely shrink the error margin, while integer descent eliminates it — this matters at the 1 km target where accumulated `g * BRICK_SIZE` error grows ~30× larger.\n\n**Status** — 35 tests pass (incl. new full-grid regression test `min_corner_inserts_land_in_distinct_leaves`), clippy and fmt clean, chasms confirmed gone by manual test. Perf AC (≥30 FPS) still to be validated — the debug HUD's GPU timestamps (17.35/17.50/17.47 ms all near-identical) look suspect on their own."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T15:19:50.365364Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-1293d8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1c7b686c-7851-43a5-9b04-65923ab96671","text":"## Summary\n\n`trace_brick` in `raymarch.wgsl` now tracks `t_local` — the DDA crossing t of the current voxel, captured from the chosen `t_max` component before increment — and returns `t_enter + entry_bias + t_local` as the hit t instead of the brick AABB entry t.\n\n## Rationale\n\n`best.t` is used both for front-to-back node culling in `trace_svo` and for ordering terrain hits against BVH object instances in `cs_main`. Returning the entry t made deep-in-brick hits look artificially close, culling neighbors with genuinely closer surfaces and wrongly occluding objects standing in front of terrain.\n\n## Status\n\nShader-only change; validated by naga at pipeline creation, workspace tests pass, rendering verified manually alongside the sw-bd0852 chasm fix. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T15:19:53.921501Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
