{"id":"sw-2ef59d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-accc3c82-3a10-45e7-8db9-4f95fbb17eb2","text":"## Summary\n\nCompute, blit, and egui passes now record into separate command encoders submitted as three command buffers in one `queue.submit` — Metal resolves pass-boundary timestamps at command-buffer granularity, so passes sharing one buffer all reported the buffer's total (and the HUD summed three copies: 241 ms displayed for an ~80 ms frame). `Raymarcher::render` was split into public `compute_pass`/`blit_pass` (old `render` kept as a wrapper).\n\n## Status\n\nMechanism verified by design + headless wall-clock agreement (bench measures ~74 ms compute at the same viewpoint the HUD called 80). Remaining: confirm the HUD shows three *different* numbers on next app launch, then close."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T19:59:57.607843Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T19:59:57.851865Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6c38dc50-75a5-4be8-ae15-b88e44e766a7","text":"## Perf baseline established (first work under this story)\n\nHeadless A/B bench harness landed (`bench_raymarch`, release, `BENCH_WORLD=large BENCH_SSE=n`): wall-clocks the compute pass alone, nothing else on the GPU. Measured at the user's 1 km flythrough viewpoint (1280×720):\n\n| Config | Median |\n|---|---|\n| base trace, shadows off | **43.8 ms** |\n| + shadows (any-hit, new) | 74.0 ms |\n| + shadows (closest-hit, old) | 78.6 ms |\n\nFindings:\n- **Shadows cost ~30 ms** — any-hit conversion recovered only ~5 ms; the shadow traversal itself is as expensive as the descent, not the hit refinement. Candidates: half-res shadow pass, distance-capped shadows, shadow ray coarse-only traversal (stop at SSE-coarse nodes).\n- **SSE threshold sweep (0.8 → 4.0) has no measurable effect** — traversal is memory-latency bound (dependent random reads into a 128 MB node buffer), not depth bound. Rules out threshold tuning as a win; points at node layout/locality (children-block ordering, node compaction, possibly a shallower wide tree or brick-level DDA entry) as the real work.\n- Budget: 43.8 ms base → ≤ 33 ms (30 fps) needs ~25% off the base trace before shadows even enter; 60 fps needs ~3×.\n\nNote: the ≥30 fps AC inherited from sw-f089de lives here now. Timestamp fix (sw-2ef59d) gives real per-pass attribution in the HUD from the next launch."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T20:00:11.748534Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2ef59d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0b60eb6d-c6ef-44e8-833c-0f32d56bfc5c","text":"User confirmed: HUD now shows distinct per-pass numbers after the end-timestamp derivation fix (`f780f7d`). Closing."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T20:06:41.715707Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
