{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T20:21:53.102738Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-21e54e30-883a-4198-aef3-60bca64c63e3","text":"## Phases 1–2 landed; Phase 3 premise falsified by measurement\n\nAll numbers: `bench_raymarch`, 1280×720, bench viewpoint, today's machine state (baseline re-measured at 49.0/83.9 ms — hotter than the recorded 43.8/74.0; all deltas are same-day A/B).\n\n### Landed (byte-identical output, verified by probe compare)\n\n| Change | shadows OFF | shadows ON |\n|---|---|---|\n| baseline (today) | 49.0 | 83.9 |\n| **Phase 1: single-read traversal** — node fields cached in stack frames, each SVO node fetched exactly once per ray (was ~k+2×) | 39.9 (−19%) | 69.7 |\n| **Phase 2: 8-byte stack frames** — integer cell coords replace stored `node_min`, 320→128 B/thread | **32.4 (−34%)** | **58.9 (−30%)** |\n\nPhase 2 probe: 3/921600 pixels differ (ulp-level `node_min` rounding — one multiply vs ten accumulated adds; new form is the more exact). Phase 1: byte-identical.\n\n### Phase 3 experiments (shader-override A/B, no rebuilds)\n\n| Experiment | shadows ON | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| shadow SSE multiplier N=4/8/16 | 58.3/59.5/56.2, probes byte-identical | **no-op** — sun at 53° + 26 m terrain: shadow rays never reach the far field where SSE coarsening bites |\n| SSE threshold 1.5/2.5/4.0 (re-sweep post-P2) | 55.9–62.2 (noise) | still not depth-bound |\n| ndotl==0 gate | 62.8 | no win (divergence/noise) |\n| stub brick DDA (diagnostic) | 50.8 | brick DDA ≈ 8 ms of shadow cost |\n| skip instance BVH (diagnostic) | 55.7 | BVH ≈ 3 ms |\n| slab clip, **correct** terrain top | **56.1, probe byte-identical** | exact −2.8 ms; worth landing (needs `terrain_top` plumbed — `u.grid_dims` is a dead uniform hardwired to 0,0,0) |\n| slab clip with the dead uniform (bug) | 30.6 | shadows silently vanished — caught by probe diff (4.6% px). Proves shadow cost is ~100% traversal, no fixed overhead; lit pixels proving \"no occluder\" are the expensive case |\n\n### Where that leaves the 33 ms budget\n\nBase 32.4 + shadows 26.5 = 58.9. Shadow cost decomposes ≈ 15.5 node descent + 8 brick DDA + 3 BVH. Every cheap lever is spent; reaching ≤33 ms with shadows needs structural work beyond the approved spec — see revised proposal (next)."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T20:42:26.268171Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T20:53:21.964509Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-93336222-2409-4ac8-8d4e-21e8281b6d09","text":"## Phase 3 progress: two more exact wins landed; quad-share tried and reverted\n\nSame-day A/B (interleaved rounds to cancel thermal drift; absolute medians swing ±15% with machine temperature, so deltas are same-round):\n\n| Landed change | base | shadows ON | image |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3a slab clip (terrain_top_y via dead `grid_dims` uniform slot) | — | −2.8 ms | byte-identical |\n| 3b occupancy masks (64-bit per brick, gate voxel reads) | ~0 | ~0 | byte-identical — brick DDA is iteration-bound, not read-bound; masks kept (near-free, enable chunk-granular tricks) |\n| 3b bit-iteration child advance (`firstTrailingBit` over flip-permuted mask replaces the 8-slot scan loop) | −3..−5 ms | −5..−9 ms | byte-identical |\n| 3b absolute AABB eps (`VOXEL_SCALE * 0.02` replaces `node_size * 0.001`) | −3..−4 ms | −4..−6 ms | 494 px (large) / 1828 px (default) isolated 1-px shading flips at grazing edges; crack-analysis clean (no runs, no sky bleed) — integer-cell node mins make parent/child planes coincide exactly, so only arithmetic rounding needs the pad |\n\nBest clean state: **~25 ms base / ~41 ms shadows ON** (from 49.0/83.9 baseline).\n\n**Tried and reverted: 2×2 quad shadow sharing** (one shadow ray per quad via workgroup memory). Only −1 ms for 0.47% pixel change — intra-warp decimation doesn't cut wall time in a latency-bound kernel: every simdgroup still stalls on its representative lanes' dependent fetches. Real half-res shadows need warp-dense packing, i.e. the separate-pass fallback (b) the user pre-authorized. Its trigger condition (3a+3b re-bench still \u003e33 ms) is now measured fact — proceeding with the 3-pass split: full-res primary → G-buffer, packed 640×360 shadow pass, full-res composite. Testing chunk-granular shadow any-hit (occupied 4³ chunk = occluder) as a compounding cheapener first."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T21:17:28.08366Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-031260","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"double_free_panics test fails under --release (should_panic on a debug_assert)","description":"`brick_pool::tests::double_free_panics` uses `#[should_panic]` to assert that `BrickPool::free` rejects a stale handle — but the check is a `debug_assert_eq!`, which compiles out in release builds, so `cargo test --release -p smallworld-engine` fails on a test that passes in debug.\n\nFound while running the full suite in release during sw-2230ee perf validation (release is the measurement profile). Not a product bug — the double-free guard is intentionally debug-only.\n\n**Fix:** gate the test with `#[cfg(debug_assertions)]` so it only runs in profiles where the guard exists.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"b0X","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-031260","target_id":"sw-2230ee","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","engine","tests"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T21:32:20.961763Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T21:44:57.935829Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-282f3c22-1d7a-4a8b-b539-7d18c3e4dfe5","text":"## Phase 3c landed: half-res shadow pass. Status at end of session — pending review\n\n**Architecture change** (`raymarcher.rs`, `raymarch.wgsl`): the monolithic kernel is now three passes — `cs_primary` (full res, trace → G-buffer: world_pos+ndotl rgba32f / albedo rgba8 / normal rgba8snorm), `cs_shadow` (half res, one ray per 2×2 quad, warp-dense; pass skipped entirely when shadows off), `cs_shade` (composite). Caller-visible API unchanged; the caller's timestamp pair is split across P1-begin/P3-end so HUD compute time still covers the whole workload.\n\n**Why a separate pass**: measured in-pass 2×2 quad sharing first — only −1 ms for the same 0.47% pixel cost, because intra-warp decimation saves work, not wall time (every simdgroup still stalls on its tracing lanes). Packed half-res is the real 4×: shadow marginal cost fell **~21 ms → ~3.5 ms** (ON−OFF, consistent across runs).\n\n**Shadow quality**: 4,339/921,600 px (0.47%) differ vs full-res shadows on the large world, 3,744 (0.41%) on Default — 2×2 quantization at shadow edges; magnified side-by-side crop generated for review (visually near-identical at native res). Awaiting user sign-off.\n\n**Where the numbers stand** (all @1280×720 bench viewpoint unless noted):\n- Session baseline → now: shadows ON **83.9 → ~35–37 ms**, OFF **49.0 → ~31–33 ms** (rested-machine run).\n- Flythrough (`--bench largeworld`, 20 s, 680 frames): **GPU avg 20.9 ms, p99 23.4 ms** — well inside the 33 ms budget along the real camera path. Frame-time p99 (47.5 ms) is CPU/streaming-bound (cpu p99 38.2), outside this story's scope per spec.\n- **Open question**: bench-viewpoint median sits ~2–4 ms above the 33 ms line, and the machine degraded into hard thermal throttling (impossible readings: shadows-OFF \u003e ON, 40% median swings) before I could resolve whether the 3-pass split's ~1 ms expected overhead is actually larger at that viewpoint. Needs one clean cool-machine A/B (split vs single-pass base) — candidates if real: pack ndotl into albedo.a so `cs_shade` does one 8-bit load, or store depth-t r32f instead of rgba32f world_pos.\n\n**Tests**: engine 30/30 release + 31/31 debug, sandbox green. Pre-existing release-profile test bug found, filed and fixed as sw-031260 (`double_free_panics` gated to `debug_assertions`)."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T21:52:12.610948Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
