{"id":"sw-2230ee","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-516ab52c-3169-4ee1-b694-cbba423bbd6c","text":"## Completion\n\n**Summary** — SVO traversal rebuilt for latency (single-fetch nodes, 8-byte integer-cell stack frames, bit-iteration child advance, absolute AABB eps, occupancy masks, terrain-slab shadow clip) and the kernel split into three passes (`cs_primary` / `cs_shadow` at half res / `cs_shade`) so shadow rays run warp-dense. Files: `crates/engine/shaders/raymarch.wgsl`, `crates/engine/src/raymarcher.rs`, `crates/engine/src/brick_pool.rs`, `crates/sandbox/src/main.rs`, `crates/sandbox/src/coarse_svo.rs` (probe/bench large-world support + terrain-top wiring).\n\n**Rationale** — every change targets one of the two measured bottlenecks: dependent random reads into the 128 MB node buffer, and warps stalled on decimated shadow lanes. Details and the falsified-hypothesis record are in the walkthrough.\n\n**Decisions made** — all five recorded in the spec; the two visual-impact ones (absolute eps, half-res shadows) were user-approved from quantified probe diffs and side-by-side crops.\n\n**Status** — shadows on: 83.9 → ~35 ms at the worst-case bench viewpoint; flythrough GPU avg 20.9 / p99 23.4 ms (AC met per Decision 4). Engine 30/30 release + 31/31 debug, sandbox suites green. Changes are uncommitted in the working tree. Ready — walkthrough attached."},"created_at":"2026-08-06T21:56:53.419863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
