{"id":"sw-58e648","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"60 fps push for the 1 km world: beam pre-pass, node re-layout, split overhead","description":"Follow-up to sw-2230ee (closed at 30 fps per user decision). The 1 km world renders at GPU avg 20.9 / p99 23.4 ms on the flythrough; 60 fps (≤16 ms) and the worst-case viewpoint need structural work:\n\n## Candidates, in expected-value order\n\n- **Beam pre-pass**: 1/8-res conservative min-t per tile; primary rays start at their tile's depth, skipping top-of-tree descent and empty-space marching. Biggest base-trace lever (ESVO-style).\n- **Split-overhead A/B on a cool machine**: single-pass vs 3-pass base trace at the bench viewpoint (end-of-session thermal throttling made this unresolvable — shadows-off measured slower than shadows-on). If the split costs \u003e ~1 ms: pack ndotl into `gbuf_albedo.a` so `cs_shade` does one 8-bit load, and/or store depth-t `r32float` instead of `rgba32float` world_pos (reconstruct position from the camera ray in `cs_shadow`).\n- **Node-buffer re-layout / compaction**: parent→child locality for the 128 MB node buffer (streaming makes this a rolling compaction).\n- **Occupancy-mask chunk skipping**: masks landed in sw-2230ee (binding 8) but the fine DDA still steps per-voxel; a true two-level DDA cuts iterations ~4× in empty space (brick cost is iteration-bound).\n\n## Context\n\n- Fixed bench viewpoint (`bench_raymarch`, BENCH_WORLD=large): ~35 ms shadows-on — the worst case, 2–4 ms over the 30 fps line.\n- Flythrough dt p99 47.5 ms is **CPU/streaming-side** (cpu p99 38.2) — a separate concern worth its own issue if hitches matter for the demo.\n\nMeasurement protocol and the full experiment matrix live in sw-2230ee's spec/comments/walkthrough.","parent_id":"sw-ff3ae3","sort_order":"b0W","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-58e648","target_id":"sw-2230ee","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","rendering","perf"]},"created_at":"2026-08-06T21:57:08.109562Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
