{"id":"sw-9bd616","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Successor to sw-ff3ae3. That epic proved the architecture (1 km × 1 km at 10 cm voxels, raytraced SVO, ≥30 fps with shadows). This spike takes it from proof-of-concept to something that stands next to battlemoon and MG's engine without apology.\n\n## Tracks\n\n**1. Performance — buy fps on the two axes that matter** (rays × steps-per-ray)\n- Cheaper rays: beam pre-pass, two-level chunk DDA, node re-layout (sw-58e648)\n- Fewer rays: temporal shadow reuse, resolution upscaling\n\n**2. Looks — close the shading gap** (reference: `notes/mg-mishmash-notes.md` + dev log screenshots)\n- Occupancy AO + coarse-grid light propagation\n- Water shading pass\n\n**3. Smooth — kill every visible LOD artifact** (the reason this project exists)\n- No hard near/far cutover, no floating coarse nodes, no LOD rings, no level color banding\n\n## Acceptance targets\n\n- Flythrough GPU p99 ≤ 16.6 ms (60 fps) at 720p render on M1 Max, shadows on\n- Stretch: 1440p output via upscaling within the same budget\n- A flythrough recording with zero visible LOD transitions at travel speed\n- Side-by-side with the MG dev log shots no longer reads as flat/unshaded\n\n## Method (inherited from sw-2230ee — see its spec/walkthrough)\n\nByte-compare probes for no-visual-change work; quantified pixel diffs + crack analysis for visual changes; interleaved same-run A/B benching (absolute medians drift ±15% with thermals); shader-override iteration via `SMALLWORLD_SHADER_DIR`; bench numbers never trusted without an image compare.","labels":["epic","rendering","perf"],"sort_order":"b0Y","status":"PLANNED","title":"Spike: 1 km world — 60 fps, modern looks, smooth LOD"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T22:22:50.785474Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
