{"id":"sw-a5e257","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5e257","target_id":"sw-449c64"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5e257","target_id":"sw-5304ba"}]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:26:02.630735Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a5e257","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5e257","target_id":"sw-449c64"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5e257","target_id":"sw-5304ba"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5e257","target_id":"sw-764a6a"}],"sort_order":"apz"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:37:12.673212Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-cf6350","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Benchmark `bevy_ecs` vs `hecs` at a few million voxel entities. Measure insert/iterate throughput, query performance, and assess WGPU resource integration ergonomics. Winner gets adopted.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Benchmark harness with reproducible insert/iterate/query measurements\n- At least 2M entities in the benchmark\n- Written comparison with recommendation\n- Decision documented","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","ecs","research","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0U","status":"BACKLOG","title":"ECS A/B spike: bevy_ecs vs hecs"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:26:17.617967Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-314e8f","target_id":"sw-cf6350"}],"description":"Adopt the ECS winner from the A/B spike. Wrap existing `Scene` (SVO, BrickPool, BVH, instances) as ECS resources and components. Engine must boot and render identically to current behavior.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- ECS crate integrated into engine Cargo.toml\n- SVO, BrickPool, BVH, camera, instances modeled as ECS resources/components\n- All existing scenes render correctly\n- No performance regression on existing benchmarks","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","ecs","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0V","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Adopt ECS and wrap existing Scene as resources/components"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:26:26.409433Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3f6bdc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Define the `VoxelVolume` trait with enough structure for traversal optimization:\n\n- `volume_type() → VolumeKind` enum (SVO, FlatGrid, ChunkedDDA) for shader dispatch\n- `traversal_bindings()` exposing type-specific GPU resources\n- `bounds()` returning world-space AABB\n- `lod_hint()` for LOD metadata\n\nThe trait exposes enough structure so renderers can dispatch optimized traversal kernels per volume type — not fully opaque.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `VoxelVolume` trait defined in engine crate\n- `VolumeKind` enum with at least SVO variant\n- Trait compiles and is usable as `dyn VoxelVolume` or generic bound\n- Documentation on trait contract","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","abstractions","volumes","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0W","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Define VoxelVolume trait with VolumeKind shader dispatch"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:26:36.110562Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-fdfee5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Dedicated GPU storage buffer for per-chunk and per-meshlet bounding boxes, separate from volume data. Packed layout optimized for culling compute passes. Populated by any `VoxelVolume` implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `AabbBuffer` struct with GPU storage buffer\n- Packed AABB layout (min.xyz, max.xyz per entry)\n- API: `alloc()`, `update()`, `free()`, `bind_group()`\n- Any `VoxelVolume` can register AABBs into it\n- Unit tests for allocation/deallocation","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","abstractions","culling","gpu-compute","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0X","status":"BACKLOG","title":"AABB buffer abstraction for GPU culling passes"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:26:43.676566Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-270c05","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"High-performance depth representation optimized for HzB construction and occlusion queries. Decoupled from render target depth so the culling pipeline can run ahead of shading.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `DepthBuffer` struct independent of swap chain / render target\n- Writable by execution stage (raytrace or rasterize)\n- Readable by culling stage for HzB pyramid construction\n- Supports previous-frame readback for temporal occlusion\n- Correct resize handling on window resize","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","abstractions","culling","depth","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0Y","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Depth buffer abstraction decoupled from render targets"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:26:51.689577Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-45a34a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Lightweight spatial hierarchy (SVO nodes or chunk grid) storing only AABBs + residency state + LOD metadata. Fits in RAM for arbitrarily large worlds. This is the OOC pipeline's source of truth for what exists in the world.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `WorldSkeleton` struct with spatial hierarchy\n- Per-cell state: `Unknown`, `Air`, `Loading`, `Resident`, `MipOnly`\n- Per-cell metadata: AABB, LOD level, residency generation\n- RAM footprint stays under 100 MB for a 10 km³ world\n- API for querying visible cells, updating residency state\n- Integrates with existing coarse SVO construction","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","abstractions","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0Z","status":"BACKLOG","title":"World skeleton: lightweight spatial hierarchy for OOC"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:01.447752Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-97e655","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Define the two execution-stage trait interfaces:\n\n**`Renderer`** trait: `prepare()`, `encode()`, `resize()`, `output_texture()`. Abstracts over raytracing and rasterization pipelines.\n\n**`MeshExtractor`** trait: `extract(volume, lod) → MeshData`. Abstracts over meshing algorithms (Marching Cubes, Dual Contouring, etc.).\n\nStub implementations for both — no real meshing yet.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Both traits defined in engine crate\n- `MeshData` struct defined (vertex + index + normal buffers)\n- Stub `MeshExtractor` that returns empty mesh\n- Traits are `Send + Sync` compatible\n- Documentation on trait contracts","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","engine","abstractions","rendering","meshing","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0a","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Define Renderer and MeshExtractor traits"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:11.105517Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-423cf8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-423cf8","target_id":"sw-3f6bdc"}],"description":"Refactor existing SVO+BrickPool into `SvoVolume` implementing `VoxelVolume`. Preserve cursor-based traversal, occupancy masks, coarse color LOD. This is the first working path through the entire OOC pipeline.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `SvoVolume` struct implementing `VoxelVolume` trait\n- All existing SVO functionality preserved (traversal, LOD, dirty tracking)\n- Populates shared AABB buffer\n- All existing scenes render identically\n- No performance regression","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","volumes","svo","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0b","status":"BACKLOG","title":"SvoVolume: wrap existing SVO+BrickPool as VoxelVolume"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:20.783058Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-9d5639","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-9d5639","target_id":"sw-3f6bdc"}],"description":"Implement `ChunkedVolume` — 32³ brick chunks in a spatial grid, macro-level skip via BVH bounding box test, DDA within each brick. Behind `VoxelVolume` trait so renderer dispatches identically to SVO. The workhorse for near-field destructible terrain.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `ChunkedVolume` implementing `VoxelVolume`\n- 32³ voxel chunks with DDA traversal shader\n- Macro-level BVH for chunk skipping\n- WGSL traversal kernel integrated into shader dispatch\n- Populates shared AABB buffer\n- Benchmark: comparable ray throughput to SVO for dense near-field","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","volumes","chunked-dda","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0c","status":"BACKLOG","title":"ChunkedVolume: 32³ brick chunks with BVH macro skip + DDA"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:30.751243Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-766bdc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-766bdc","target_id":"sw-3f6bdc"}],"description":"Implement `FlatGrid` volume — uniform 3D array, DDA traversal shader. For small props and as a benchmark baseline against SVO and ChunkedDDA.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `FlatGrid` implementing `VoxelVolume`\n- Simple DDA traversal shader\n- Populates shared AABB buffer\n- Works for VoxelModel instances (trees, rocks, props)\n- Benchmark results vs SVO and ChunkedVolume","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","volumes","flat-grid","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0d","status":"BACKLOG","title":"FlatGrid volume: uniform 3D array with DDA traversal"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:40.524069Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-5c29a8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Generalize BVH from instance-only to a reusable spatial acceleration structure. `BvhAccel\u003cT: Bounded\u003e` usable by ChunkedVolume macro structure, the instance system, and meshlet culling.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Generic `BvhAccel\u003cT: Bounded\u003e` struct\n- `Bounded` trait: `fn aabb(\u0026self) → Aabb`\n- Existing instance BVH migrated to use new generic\n- ChunkedVolume can use it for macro-level skip\n- No performance regression on instance traversal","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","acceleration","bvh","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0e","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Generalize BVH to BvhAccel\u0026lt;T: Bounded\u0026gt;"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:49.154067Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-823731","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Extend the brick data format to store per-edge Hermite intersection points and surface normals alongside existing palette voxels. Required for Dual Contouring mesh extraction.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `BrickDataExt` or extended `BrickData` with Hermite fields\n- Per-edge intersection position (3 edges per voxel × 16³)\n- Per-edge surface normal\n- GPU-friendly alignment (4-byte or 16-byte boundaries)\n- Streaming-compatible layout (fits in ring buffer segments)\n- Backward-compatible: existing bricks without Hermite data still work\n- Memory budget analysis documented","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","volumes","brick-data","hermite","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0f","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Extended brick data: Hermite intersections + surface normals"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:27:58.134803Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-7b4d1c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Split the thread pool into dedicated I/O threads (disk read + zstd decompress) vs. compute threads (worldgen, meshing). Sized independently. Replaces ad-hoc thread spawning in the pager.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `ThreadPool` with separate I/O and compute pools\n- I/O pool: 2-3 threads for disk reads + decompression\n- Compute pool: 4-6 threads for worldgen + meshing\n- Pools sized independently at engine init\n- Replaces current crossbeam thread spawning in BrickPager\n- No stutter from I/O blocking compute or vice versa","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","streaming","concurrency","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0g","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Split thread pool: dedicated I/O vs compute workers"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:28:07.123629Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-7ec837","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-7ec837","target_id":"sw-7b4d1c"}],"description":"Wire `BrickSource` trait, GPU worldgen, CPU worldgen fallback, and zstd region cache into the OOC resolve stage. Thread pool workers fill `VoxelVolume` instances on demand from seed or disk.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `BrickSource` implementations (GPU gen, CPU gen, disk cache) wired to thread pool\n- VoxelVolume instances populated by resolve stage\n- GPU worldgen used as primary, CPU as fallback\n- Region cache read/write through I/O thread pool\n- End-to-end: seed → generate → VoxelVolume → renderable","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","streaming","worldgen","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0h","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Integrate data sources into OOC resolve stage"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:28:16.167623Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b6a4cf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"GPU benchmark harness comparing ray throughput (Mrays/s) across all `VoxelVolume` types at matched world content. Serves as a regression gate for future changes.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Benchmark binary or mode in sandbox\n- Test same terrain content across SVO, ChunkedDDA, FlatGrid\n- Measure Mrays/s, frame time, GPU pass times\n- Results output as structured data (JSON or table)\n- CI-friendly: can run headless with pass/fail threshold\n- Baseline numbers documented","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","benchmark","volumes","perf","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-764a6a","sort_order":"b0i","status":"BACKLOG","title":"GPU benchmark harness: volume type ray throughput comparison"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:28:24.650672Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-97f0c9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-97f0c9","target_id":"sw-fdfee5"}],"description":"GPU compute pass testing AABB buffer entries against camera frustum planes. Output: visibility bitfield marking surviving cells.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Compute shader reading AABB buffer + camera frustum uniforms\n- Output visibility bitfield (1 bit per AABB entry)\n- Frustum extracted from view-projection matrix\n- 6-plane test with early-out\n- Benchmark: cull 100k+ AABBs in \u003c 0.1ms","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","culling","frustum","gpu-compute","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-2e26ca","sort_order":"b0j","status":"BACKLOG","title":"GPU frustum culler: AABB vs camera frustum planes"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:28:33.986078Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-9c59e9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-9c59e9","target_id":"sw-270c05"}],"description":"Build mip-chain depth pyramid from previous frame's depth buffer output. Compute shader, power-of-two downsample. Each mip level stores the maximum depth of its 2×2 parent region.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Compute shader generating full mip chain from depth buffer\n- Power-of-two downsample (max of 2×2 → 1 texel per level)\n- Texture stored as R32Float mip chain\n- Handles non-power-of-two source resolutions\n- Correct on window resize\n- Benchmark: full pyramid construction \u003c 0.1ms","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","culling","hzb","gpu-compute","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-2e26ca","sort_order":"b0k","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Hierarchical Z-Buffer: mip-chain depth pyramid construction"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:28:46.382027Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-5f048d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-5f048d","target_id":"sw-97f0c9"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-5f048d","target_id":"sw-9c59e9"}],"description":"Test frustum-surviving AABBs against the HzB pyramid. Conservative screen-space AABB projection, sample coarsest mip level that covers the projection. Cells behind opaque geometry are culled.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Compute shader: project AABB to screen-space rect\n- Select mip level where rect fits in a single texel\n- Compare AABB near-Z against HzB depth at that mip\n- Conservative: never cull something that should be visible\n- Output: updated visibility bitfield (frustum ∩ occlusion)\n- Benchmark: cull 100k+ AABBs in \u003c 0.2ms total (frustum + occlusion)","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","culling","occlusion","gpu-compute","critical","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-2e26ca","sort_order":"b0l","status":"BACKLOG","title":"GPU occlusion culler: AABB vs HzB test"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:28:55.139163Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-1d4df7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Move per-chunk SSE evaluation from CPU (`BrickPager::classify_demand`) into the culling compute pass. Unified visibility + LOD decision in one dispatch.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- SSE computed per-AABB in the same compute pass as culling\n- `voxel_scale × focal_length / distance` calculation on GPU\n- Output: per-cell LOD classification (coarse/fine/evict)\n- CPU-side `classify_demand` removed or reduced to reading GPU results\n- No visual difference from current SSE-driven LOD","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","culling","sse","lod","gpu-compute","refactor","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-2e26ca","sort_order":"b0m","status":"BACKLOG","title":"GPU SSE evaluator: move LOD classification to culling pass"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:29:03.493895Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-403ae6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-403ae6","target_id":"sw-5f048d"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-403ae6","target_id":"sw-1d4df7"}],"description":"Feed GPU culling results back to CPU. Diff the visible set against the resident set to emit stream requests (visible + high-SSE + not-yet-resident) and eviction candidates (not visible + low priority).\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- GPU → CPU readback of visibility + SSE results\n- Diff engine: compare visible set vs resident set\n- Output: prioritized stream request list\n- Output: eviction candidate list\n- Latency: readback completes within 1 frame\n- Cancellation: loads for newly-culled cells cancelled","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","culling","ooc-pipeline","streaming","critical","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-2e26ca","sort_order":"b0n","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Visibility readback: feed culling results to streaming stage"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:29:12.429945Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-acac64","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Fixed-size cyclic upload heap with per-segment locking and wraparound. Replace current per-brick `write_buffer` calls. Workers lock a segment, write vertex/voxel data, release.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `RingBuffer` struct with configurable total size\n- Segment allocation: `alloc(size) → Option\u003cSegment\u003e`\n- Segment locking: prevents overwrite until freed\n- Wraparound: allocates from start when end reached\n- Thread-safe: multiple workers can lock segments concurrently\n- Replaces all `queue.write_buffer()` calls in brick upload path\n- Benchmark: throughput vs current per-brick writes","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","streaming","gpu-transfer","ring-buffer","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-e74f7a","sort_order":"b0o","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Ring buffer allocator: cyclic CPU→GPU staging heap"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:29:22.487065Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ee4601","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-ee4601","target_id":"sw-acac64"}],"description":"Metal-specific copy path: cyclic `MTLBuffer` sized for N frames in flight. `MTLBlitCommandEncoder` for fast `copyFromBuffer` transfers. `dispatch_semaphore` / frame-in-flight counter prevents CPU overwriting segments the GPU is still reading.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Ring buffer backed by `MTLBuffer` in shared/managed memory\n- N-frame-in-flight sizing (typically 3)\n- Blit command encoder for staging → VRAM copies\n- `dispatch_semaphore` gating segment recycling\n- CPU never overwrites a segment GPU is reading\n- Verified on Apple Silicon (unified memory path)\n- Frame time: no stalls from copy operations","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","streaming","gpu-transfer","metal","critical","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-e74f7a","sort_order":"b0p","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Metal copy path: MTLBuffer ring + blit encoder + semaphore"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:29:32.138905Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a9803f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a9803f","target_id":"sw-acac64"}],"description":"Vulkan-specific async transfer path: dedicated transfer queue where available. Fence insertion after copy submission, poll on next frame, recycle staging segments only after GPU confirms transfer complete.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Detect and use dedicated transfer queue family\n- Fallback to graphics queue if no transfer queue\n- Fence insertion per copy batch\n- Fence polling on subsequent frames\n- Staging segment recycled only after fence signals\n- No transfer stalls on graphics queue","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","streaming","gpu-transfer","vulkan","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-e74f7a","sort_order":"b0q","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Vulkan async transfer: dedicated queue + fence recycling"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:29:42.360403Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-f2e207","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-f2e207","target_id":"sw-403ae6"}],"description":"Visibility-aware priority ordering for load requests: (visible × SSE) priority score. Cancellation tokens for loads that become irrelevant when camera moves. Integrates with culling stage visibility output.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `LoadQueue` with priority ordering by visibility × SSE\n- Cancellation tokens: cancel in-flight loads for cells that leave visible set\n- Integration with visibility readback from E3\n- Starvation prevention: low-priority loads still make progress\n- Metrics: queue depth, cancellation rate, average wait time","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","streaming","ooc-pipeline","scheduling","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-e74f7a","sort_order":"b0r","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Priority queue for load requests with cancellation tokens"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:29:52.77234Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2d5e8f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Enforce hard VRAM and RAM budgets. Eviction policy: LRU weighted by SSE and visibility age. Panic eviction path for sudden camera teleports that need fast memory reclamation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Configurable VRAM and RAM budget limits\n- LRU eviction weighted by SSE × visibility recency\n- Panic eviction: bulk-free lowest-priority cells on budget overrun\n- Teleport detection: sudden large camera displacement triggers panic path\n- Metrics: budget utilization, eviction rate, panic events\n- Never exceed budget: hard cap enforced before allocation","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","streaming","ooc-pipeline","memory","phase-2"],"parent_id":"sw-e74f7a","sort_order":"b0s","status":"BACKLOG","title":"VRAM/RAM budget controller with LRU eviction"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:30:01.955984Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-0f1eb5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-0f1eb5","target_id":"sw-97e655"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-0f1eb5","target_id":"sw-3f6bdc"}],"description":"Refactor existing `Raymarcher` to implement the `Renderer` trait. Consume `VoxelVolume` via `traversal_bindings()`. Dispatch traversal kernel by `VolumeKind`.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `Raymarcher` implements `Renderer` trait\n- Consumes `VoxelVolume` through trait interface\n- All existing render passes (primary, shadow, shade, blit) preserved\n- No visual or performance regression\n- Can be swapped with other `Renderer` implementations at runtime","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","raytracing","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-5304ba","sort_order":"b0t","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Refactor Raymarcher behind Renderer trait"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:30:11.368177Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-c400bc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-c400bc","target_id":"sw-0f1eb5"}],"description":"Wire the refactored raytracer as the default execution stage in the OOC pipeline. Raytrace what's resident, show coarse SVO color for what's still loading. Depth buffer output feeds back to Stage 2 HzB for next frame — this closes the pipeline's feedback loop.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Raytracer invoked by OOC pipeline execute stage\n- Coarse fallback: cells not yet resident render at SVO mip color\n- Depth buffer written to shared `DepthBuffer` abstraction\n- Depth available for next frame's HzB construction\n- Full pipeline runs end-to-end: resolve → (trivial cull) → (existing stream) → execute","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","raytracing","rendering","refactor","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-5304ba","sort_order":"b0u","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Wire raytracer as default OOC execution stage"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:30:21.188703Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3c812f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-3c812f","target_id":"sw-0f1eb5"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-3c812f","target_id":"sw-423cf8"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-3c812f","target_id":"sw-9d5639"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-3c812f","target_id":"sw-766bdc"}],"description":"Ensure SVO cursor traversal, ChunkedDDA BVH+DDA traversal, and FlatGrid DDA traversal all dispatch correctly from a single compute entry point based on `VolumeKind`.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- WGSL shader dispatches to correct traversal function per VolumeKind\n- SVO: existing cursor-based octree descent\n- ChunkedDDA: BVH macro skip → DDA micro traversal\n- FlatGrid: simple DDA traversal\n- All volume types render correctly in the same scene\n- No significant overhead from dispatch indirection","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","raytracing","shaders","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-5304ba","sort_order":"b0v","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Volume-type shader variants: SVO, ChunkedDDA, FlatGrid dispatch"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:30:30.467437Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-8b3ebc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-8b3ebc","target_id":"sw-97e655"}],"description":"Implement Marching Cubes as a `MeshExtractor`. Classic isosurface extraction from density field. Per-brick vertex + index buffer + normals output. Baseline mesh quality for the rasterization pipeline.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `MarchingCubesExtractor` implementing `MeshExtractor`\n- Standard 256-entry lookup table\n- Per-brick extraction producing `MeshData`\n- Vertex normals from gradient estimation\n- Material/palette color per vertex\n- Handles brick boundaries (samples neighbors)\n- Visual quality: smooth terrain surfaces","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","meshing","marching-cubes","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b0w","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Marching Cubes mesh extractor"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:30:46.344991Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a5105c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5105c","target_id":"sw-97e655"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a5105c","target_id":"sw-823731"}],"description":"Implement Dual Contouring as a `MeshExtractor`. Preserves sharp edges from Hermite data (edge intersections + surface normals stored in extended brick data from E2.5). Higher quality for architectural and blocky content.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `DualContouringExtractor` implementing `MeshExtractor`\n- Reads Hermite intersection + normal data from extended bricks\n- QEF (Quadric Error Function) minimization for vertex placement\n- Sharp edge preservation on blocky/architectural geometry\n- Handles brick boundaries\n- Visual quality: crisp edges on cubes, smooth on organic terrain","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","meshing","dual-contouring","hermite","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b0x","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Dual Contouring mesh extractor"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:30:56.459368Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a350a2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-a350a2","target_id":"sw-8b3ebc"}],"description":"Cluster extracted meshes into 64–128 triangle meshlets and build a DAG hierarchy for LOD. Evaluate `meshoptimizer` crate first for clustering + simplification. If it integrates cleanly, use it. If it creates too much churn in our codebase, roll our own Nanite-style pipeline.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Meshes decomposed into 64–128 triangle meshlets\n- Per-meshlet bounding sphere + normal cone for culling\n- LOD DAG: parent meshlets are simplified versions of children\n- At least 3 LOD levels in the DAG\n- `meshoptimizer` evaluation documented (decision + rationale)\n- Memory overhead per meshlet documented","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","engine","meshing","meshlets","lod","critical","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b0y","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Meshlet decomposition: meshoptimizer or own Nanite pipeline"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:31:06.051803Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-d5984e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-d5984e","target_id":"sw-a350a2"}],"description":"GPU compute pass: per-meshlet SSE check against camera. Output indirect draw buffer selecting parent (coarse) or children (fine) meshlets based on screen-space error threshold.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Compute shader evaluating SSE per meshlet\n- DAG traversal: select coarsest meshlet that satisfies SSE threshold\n- Output: indirect draw commands for selected meshlets\n- No popping: seamless LOD transition at threshold boundary\n- Benchmark: evaluate 100k+ meshlets in \u003c 0.2ms","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","meshing","meshlets","sse","lod","gpu-compute","critical","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b0z","status":"BACKLOG","title":"GPU meshlet SSE evaluator: per-meshlet LOD selection"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:31:14.753347Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-5e2e3d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-5e2e3d","target_id":"sw-d5984e"}],"description":"Implement LOD transition strategies to eliminate popping:\n\n- **Geomorphing**: vertex interpolation between LOD levels during transition\n- **Dithered blending**: screen-door dissolve pattern fading between LODs\n\nSelectable per-material.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Geomorphing: smooth vertex morph over configurable transition distance\n- Dithered: Bayer matrix dissolve pattern\n- Per-material selection (material metadata flag)\n- No visible pop at LOD boundaries\n- Performance: \u003c 5% overhead vs hard LOD switch","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","meshing","lod","rendering","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b10","status":"BACKLOG","title":"LOD transitions: geomorphing and dithered blending"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:31:23.760733Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-befc76","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-befc76","target_id":"sw-8b3ebc"}],"description":"Seal cracks between adjacent chunks at different LOD levels using Transvoxel transition cells or geometry skirt generation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- No visible cracks at chunk LOD boundaries\n- Transvoxel transition cells OR downward skirts (evaluate both, pick one)\n- Handles all 6 face directions of a chunk\n- Performance: \u003c 10% additional triangles vs base mesh\n- Works with both Marching Cubes and Dual Contouring output","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","meshing","lod","stitching","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b11","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Chunk boundary stitching: Transvoxel or skirt generation"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:31:32.582013Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-97bd1a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-97bd1a","target_id":"sw-97e655"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-97bd1a","target_id":"sw-d5984e"}],"description":"Implement the rasterization `Renderer`. Vertex/fragment pipeline with G-buffer output matching raytracer format (position, albedo, normal). GPU-driven indirect rendering: meshlet SSE output feeds indirect draw commands. Single `draw_indexed_indirect` per material, no CPU draw call submission.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- `Rasterizer` implementing `Renderer` trait\n- Vertex + fragment shaders writing G-buffer (position, albedo, normal)\n- G-buffer format matches raytracer output for compositor compatibility\n- Indirect draw from meshlet SSE compute output\n- Depth buffer written to shared `DepthBuffer` abstraction\n- No per-draw-call CPU overhead\n- Benchmark: triangle throughput at 1M+ triangles","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","rasterization","gpu-driven","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b12","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Rasterizer: Renderer trait + GPU-driven indirect rendering"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:31:46.489095Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-4f73ac","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-4f73ac","target_id":"sw-97bd1a"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-4f73ac","target_id":"sw-0f1eb5"}],"description":"Compositor pass merging raytracer output (GI, shadows, distant terrain) with rasterizer output (near terrain, objects). Depth-aware blending with shared lighting model. This is where the hybrid engine produces its final frame.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Compute or fragment shader compositing two G-buffers\n- Depth-aware: closer surface wins at each pixel\n- Shared lighting: same ambient, sun direction, shadow model\n- Seamless boundary: no visible seam between raytraced and rasterized regions\n- Performance: composition pass \u003c 0.5ms at 1080p","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","compositor","hybrid","critical","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b13","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Compositor: merge raytrace + rasterize output"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:31:57.698025Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-1b6e78","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-1b6e78","target_id":"sw-4f73ac"}],"description":"Configurable pipeline modes: raytrace-only (current behavior), rasterize-only, hybrid. Runtime switchable for profiling and debugging. Per-frame profiling counters surfaced in egui overlay.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- Runtime mode switching via egui toggle or hotkey\n- Modes: raytrace-only, rasterize-only, hybrid\n- Per-frame counters in egui overlay:\n  - Bricks: resident / visible / streaming / evicted\n  - Mesh cache: hit rate, meshlet count\n  - Ring buffer: utilization %\n  - Per-pass GPU timing\n- No overhead when counters are disabled","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","ooc-pipeline","profiling","debug","phase-3"],"parent_id":"sw-a5e257","sort_order":"b14","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Pipeline mode switching + profiling counters"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:32:06.761331Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
