{"id":"sw-cf6350","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"generic","filename":"ecs-comparison.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:01:38.914967Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-cf6350","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8989f638-c4fc-4f23-ae02-6db66429cff7","text":"**Summary** — Created `crates/bench-ecs/` with a standalone benchmark harness comparing `bevy_ecs` 0.19 and `hecs` 0.11 at 2M entities. Five benchmarks (bulk insert, dense iterate, sparse iterate, filtered query, component churn) plus a qualitative WGPU ergonomics probe.\n\n**Rationale** — Components sized to match real engine types (`Mat4` transform, `Vec3` AABB, `u32` brick handle) so cache behavior reflects production access patterns. Simple `Instant::now()` median-of-10 timing — no criterion overhead for a one-shot spike.\n\n**Decisions made** — Defined component types separately per module (bevy_ecs requires `#[derive(Component)]`, hecs doesn't) rather than shared types with cfg-gating. Collected entity IDs during spawn rather than querying them back, since hecs 0.11 changed its iterator API.\n\n**Recommendation** — **hecs**. Wins 4/5 benchmarks (bulk insert 1.26×, dense iterate 1.08×, filtered query 1.08×, component churn 1.40×). bevy_ecs wins sparse iteration (1.25×) but that's not the hot path. hecs is minimal, stable, and doesn't impose framework opinions on our render loop.\n\n**Status** — benchmarks passing, comparison artifact attached, ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:01:54.480155Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-cf6350","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"generic","filename":"ecs-comparison.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:17:15.954623Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
