{"id":"sw-cf6350","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:21:03.778337Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Refactor the current `Scene` (flat `Vec\u003cVoxelModel\u003e` + `Vec\u003cVoxelInstance\u003e`) into a `SlotMap`-based entity system with side structs for GPU resources. No ECS dependency — ECS adoption deferred until entity heterogeneity justifies it (game layer, material diversity).\n\n### Motivation\n\nThe ECS spike (sw-cf6350) showed that current and near-term workloads (culling, LOD, streaming, GPU upload) are all dense iteration or spatial traversal. ECS subset queries add value only when entity types diversify, which is months away. A SlotMap gives us stable entity handles, O(1) insert/remove, and dense iteration without the 36% overhead or archetype migration penalties.\n\n### Scope\n- Replace `Vec\u003cVoxelInstance\u003e` with `SlotMap\u003cEntityId, Instance\u003e` for stable handles\n- Keep `Vec\u003cVoxelModel\u003e` (shared data, referenced by handle)\n- GPU singletons (GpuContext, BrickPool, SVO, Raymarcher, etc.) stay as side structs\n- Camera stays as a standalone struct\n- BVH rebuilt from SlotMap iteration\n- All existing scenes render identically\n- No performance regression\n\n### Non-goals\n- No ECS dependency (deferred to game layer milestone)\n- No new component/query abstractions\"","labels":["feature","engine","refactor","phase-1"],"title":"Refactor Scene into SlotMap + side structs"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:25:27.735962Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:28:25.510175Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:46:07.066368Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Introduce `World` as the engine's central data structure. Owns entity instances (SlotMap with stable handles), shared models (Vec), and an extraction boundary (`extract()`) that packs world state into GPU-ready buffers. Dirty tracking built in from day one. Retires the current `Scene` struct.\n\nFollows the pattern from Unity/Unreal/Godot: game code mutates the World, the renderer consumes an extracted snapshot, the two never share mutable state.\n\n### Scope\n- `World` struct with `SlotMap\u003cInstanceKey, Instance\u003e` and `Vec\u003cVoxelModel\u003e`\n- `Instance` with position, rotation, model ref, and per-instance generation counter\n- `WorldGpuData` — the extraction output (packed GPU buffers + BVH)\n- `extract(\u0026device)` as the boundary: checks dirty flag, rebuilds when needed\n- Raymarcher migrated to consume `\u0026WorldGpuData` instead of `\u0026Scene`\n- `Scene` module removed\n- All existing scenes render identically, no performance regression\n\n### Non-goals\n- No ECS dependency\n- No incremental extract (full rebuild when dirty; mechanism in place for future optimization)\n- No spatial hierarchy yet (sw-45a34a)\"","title":"Introduce World struct with SlotMap instances and extraction boundary"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:46:20.181441Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:50:42.476522Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e","status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T10:26:32.666175Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-314e8f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-76d321a2-8380-48f2-b9c1-fff876165932","text":"**Summary** — Introduced `World` as the engine's central data structure, replacing `Scene`. `World` owns instances via `SlotMap\u003cInstanceKey, VoxelInstance\u003e`, models via `Vec\u003cVoxelModel\u003e`, and clones the `wgpu::Device` at construction so `extract()` takes no arguments. `WorldGpuData` is the renderer-facing snapshot with `instance_buffer()`, `grid_buffer()`, `bvh_buffer()`, `instance_count()`, and a `generation()` counter. The extraction boundary skips work when `dirty` is false.\n\n**Rationale** — Follows the Unity/Unreal/Godot pattern: game code mutates the World, the renderer consumes an extracted snapshot, the two never share mutable state. `SlotMap` provides stable handles for future runtime add/remove. Device stored on World eliminates the need to thread `\u0026device` through every call.\n\n**Decisions made** — Fixed a pre-existing duplicated `#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` attribute in `raymarcher.rs`. Added `#![allow(dead_code)]` to `bench-ecs` crate (intentional struct sizing fields).\n\n**Status** — `make lint` clean, `make test` passes (41 tests), `scene.rs` deleted. Ready for visual check and review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T10:35:22.317775Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
