{"id":"sw-3f6bdc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f2629390-dcf0-4c44-99dd-ba998e763c57","text":"**Summary** — Created `volume.rs` with `VoxelVolume` trait, `VolumeKind` enum (`SVO`, `FlatGrid`, `ChunkedDDA`), `AABB` (GPU-native, 32 bytes, bytemuck), `LODMeta`, and `TraversalBindings`. Migrated `bvh::build` and `World::extract` from `(Vec3, Vec3)` tuples to `AABB`. Acronyms kept capitalized per engine convention with `#[allow(clippy::upper_case_acronyms)]`.\n\n**Rationale** — `AABB` is `#[repr(C)]` + `bytemuck::Pod` from day one so it's directly uploadable to the AABB buffer (sw-fdfee5) without conversion. The trait is object-safe (`dyn VoxelVolume`) for heterogeneous volume collections. `TraversalBindings` uses a buffer slice rather than typed enum — the renderer already knows per-kind layout.\n\n**Decisions made** — No trait implementations yet (existing `Svo` and `VoxelModel` don't implement `VoxelVolume` — that's future work). `From\u003c(Vec3, Vec3)\u003e` on `AABB` for ergonomic migration of existing code.\n\n**Status** — 47 tests passing (6 new), `make lint` clean, ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T10:48:46.041477Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-de79da","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-de79da","target_id":"sw-314e8f"}],"description":"Introduce an `Engine` struct that owns all GPU plumbing (GpuContext, Surface, window) and exposes an intent-based API to game developers. Games describe what they want (windowed, resolution, vsync); the engine handles initialization and runtime changes internally.\n\n### Motivation\n\nCurrently games must manually create and thread `GpuContext`, `Surface`, `Device`, `Queue` references through every engine call. This leaks wgpu internals into the game-facing API. Game developers should never see a `wgpu::Surface` or pass `\u0026device` — they describe intent, the engine does the rest.\n\n### Scope\n- `Engine` struct owning `GpuContext`, `Surface`, window handle\n- `EngineConfig` / `WindowMode` for initialization (windowed/fullscreen, resolution, vsync)\n- Runtime surface mutation: `set_window_mode()`, `set_resolution()`, `set_vsync()`\n- Engine handles resize cascade internally (surface reconfig, render targets, etc.)\n- `World::new(\u0026engine)` instead of `World::new(\u0026device)`\n- Migrate sandbox to use `Engine` instead of manual wiring\n- Headless mode as config option, not separate code path\n\n### Non-goals\n- Full game loop abstraction (engine.run with callbacks) — future work\n- Input handling abstraction — future work","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","api","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0b","status":"PLANNED","title":"Engine struct: intent-based game-facing API"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:03:09.75458Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
