{"id":"sw-de79da","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-98682ed0-4dcd-4986-be10-1b0aaeb602a8","text":"**Summary** — Introduced `Engine` struct owning all GPU plumbing (GpuContext, DisplaySurface, cached WorldGpuData). `World` is now pure CPU data — `World::new()` takes no args, no wgpu dependency. `begin_frame(\u0026mut World)` handles extraction automatically when dirty. `FrameContext` wraps surface texture. Old sandbox renamed to `sandbox_old` as reference; new sandbox built from scratch using Engine API — boots, renders dark blue, handles resize.\n\n**Rationale** — Game developers should describe intent (window mode, resolution), never pass wgpu handles. Matches Godot's server model: scene tree is pure data, RenderingServer owns GPU state. Building a new sandbox from scratch avoids repeated migration churn.\n\n**Decisions made** — Kept old sandbox as `sandbox_old` outside workspace for visual reference. New sandbox is minimal (145 lines) — grows from here as engine features land. `Engine::headless()` for CI. `pollster` and `winit` added to engine deps.\n\n**Status** — fmt/clippy/tests clean (37 tests). New sandbox boots and renders. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:28:27.129769Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
