{"id":"sw-de79da","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:47:46.470238Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-217282","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-217282","target_id":"sw-de79da"}],"description":"Add an `Input` struct to Engine that captures keyboard, mouse, and gamepad state at the start of each frame. The update function polls it — `engine.input().key_held(KeyCode::W)`, `engine.input().mouse_delta()`. No events, no callbacks, just a stable snapshot.\n\n### Motivation\n\nThe update function currently has no way to read user input. Every major engine (Unity `Input.GetKey`, Unreal `IsInputKeyDown`, Godot `Input.is_action_pressed`) converges on the same pattern: snapshot captured at frame start, polled during update, stable for the entire frame.\n\n### Scope\n- `Input` struct with keyboard state (pressed/held/released), mouse position, mouse delta, mouse buttons\n- Engine captures winit events into `Input` between frames\n- `engine.input()` accessor returning `\u0026Input`\n- Migrate sandbox to use input for camera movement\n- Gamepad support deferred\n\n### Design note\nThe snapshot model means `Input` is a plain struct of bools and floats — no locks, no events, no callbacks. Engine writes it once at frame start, update reads it freely.\"","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","input","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0b","status":"PLANNED","title":"Input snapshot: frame-captured input state for update"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:48:01.117276Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
