{"id":"sw-217282","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:51:54.797423Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-217282","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-61e102ea-93b6-45a9-a245-9dc1aa3de975","text":"**Summary** — Added `input.rs` with `Input` struct (keyboard held/pressed/released, mouse position/delta/buttons, controller placeholder) and `ControllerState` (numbered axes + buttons). Engine captures winit events between frames and snapshots before calling update. Sandbox uses input for WASD camera movement + right-click mouse look.\n\n**Rationale** — Snapshot-at-frame-start model matches Unity/Unreal/Godot. Input is synchronous (OS requirement + consistency guarantee), unlike OOC heavy work which is async. Controllers use numbered axes/buttons (generic, not gamepad-specific) so joysticks, wheels, flight sticks all fit the same model.\n\n**Decisions made** — `controller()` returns `Option\u003c\u0026ControllerState\u003e` instead of a static default (can't construct `HashSet` in const context, and `Option` is more honest). Re-exports `winit::keyboard::KeyCode` and `winit::event::MouseButton` so games don't need direct winit dependency. Escape-to-quit stays in engine, not in input snapshot.\n\n**Status** — 41 tests passing (4 new), `make lint` clean, sandbox boots with camera movement. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:56:30.534765Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
