{"id":"sw-251ed4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-251ed4","target_id":"sw-de79da"}],"description":"Structured engine logging with log levels. The engine logs its boot/init phases (adapter selected, surface configured, renderer initialized), game loop start, and per-frame diagnostics at trace level. Games configure the log level via `EngineConfig`.\n\n### Scope\n- Engine logs boot phases: GPU adapter, surface format, renderer init, thread pool (when added)\n- Engine logs game loop start\n- Per-frame trace logging (FPS, dt) behind trace level\n- `EngineConfig` gains a `log_level` field (default: Info)\n- Engine initializes the logger — games don't call `env_logger::init()` manually\n- Structured log output (timestamp, level, module path)","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","engine","logging","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0b","status":"PLANNED","title":"Engine boot logging and log levels"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T12:43:58.668394Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-b87f8e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-b87f8e","target_id":"sw-de79da"}],"description":"Persistent worker pool initialized at engine boot. No per-task thread spawning. The pool serves the OOC streaming pipeline (worldgen, meshing, I/O) and future game jobs (AI, pathfinding).\n\n### Motivation\n\nDESIGN.md specifies split pools sized independently: I/O pool (2-3 threads) for disk reads + decompression, compute pool (4-6 threads) for worldgen + meshing. Both are partitions of a general-purpose job system. The existing `BrickPager` spawns its own threads — this replaces that with engine-managed infrastructure.\n\n### Scope\n- `ThreadPool` struct with priority queues and work-stealing\n- Initialized at engine boot, sized from `EngineConfig`\n- `engine.jobs()` accessor for submitting work from game update\n- Completion channel: workers send results, update drains them\n- Main thread (update) is the only thing that mutates World — workers produce data, update integrates\n- Migrate BrickPager to use the pool (or stub the integration for now)\n\n### Non-goals\n- Full dependency graph / topological sort — future work\n- GPU async transfer queue integration — future work\"","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","jobs","concurrency","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-449c64","sort_order":"b0c","status":"PLANNED","title":"Thread pool: persistent worker pool for OOC pipeline"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T12:44:12.340589Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
