{"id":"sw-449c64","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T15:53:13.973916Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"sw-fb5789","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"E1.5: OOC Pipeline Skeleton","description":"## OOC Pipeline: End-to-End Skeleton\n\nWire up the six-stage OOC pipeline with concrete types flowing between stages. Each stage has a real interface but a no-op/passthrough implementation. The pipeline runs every frame inside Engine::render_frame.\n\n### Pipeline\n\n```\nResolve → Submit → Cull → Mesh → Upload → Execute\n```\n\n1. **Resolve** — game generates voxel data on engine's job pool, produces VoxelVolume\n2. **Submit** — game hands volume to engine via World\n3. **Cull** — engine decides what's visible (initially: everything visible)\n4. **Mesh** — engine extracts triangles from visible volumes\n5. **Upload** — engine stages mesh data to GPU buffers\n6. **Execute** — engine rasterizes and presents\n\n### Goal\n\nData flows end-to-end. Each stage receives the right types and passes the right ones to the next. Concrete implementations (real culling, greedy meshing, ring buffers) come in E2-E6. This epic establishes the pipeline's spine.\n\n### Dependencies\n- Depends on E1 for Engine, World, VoxelVolume, JobPool","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-fb5789","target_id":"sw-449c64","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["epic","engine","ooc-pipeline","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:02:16.536147Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2985d8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pipeline stage 1: Resolve — VoxelVolume from worldgen","description":"Define the Resolve stage interface. The game submits worldgen jobs to the engine's pool, results populate a VoxelVolume. For now: a simple flat brick grid generated on the job pool and returned as a VoxelVolume implementation.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `ResolveOutput` type: the data a resolve job produces (brick data for a grid cell)\n- A concrete VoxelVolume implementation that can be populated from resolve output (FlatBrickVolume or similar)\n- Sandbox worldgen running on engine.jobs(), producing resolve output\n- Integration: sandbox submits worldgen jobs, drains results, populates volume","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a1","labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","resolve","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:02:27.696704Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-7fe21e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pipeline stage 2: Submit — World accepts volumes","description":"Define the Submit stage. The game hands populated VoxelVolumes to the World. The World stores them and marks itself dirty so the engine knows new data arrived.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `World::add_volume()` / `World::set_terrain_volume()` API\n- World stores one or more VoxelVolume trait objects (or concrete types)\n- Adding/replacing a volume marks World dirty\n- Engine's render_frame sees the volume in World and passes it to the next stage","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a2","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-7fe21e","target_id":"sw-2985d8","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","submit","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:02:36.886664Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-59c80a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pipeline stage 3: Cull — visibility determination (no-op pass)","description":"Define the Cull stage interface. Takes the submitted volumes and camera view, outputs a visibility set — which chunks/cells need rendering. Initial implementation: everything is visible (passthrough).\n\n### Deliverables\n- `VisibilitySet` type: identifies which parts of a volume are visible\n- Cull stage receives volumes + ViewState, produces VisibilitySet\n- No-op implementation: marks everything visible\n- Wired into Engine::render_frame between submit and mesh stages\n- Interface is ready for frustum culling, HzB occlusion, SSE evaluation later","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a3","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-59c80a","target_id":"sw-7fe21e","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","culling","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:02:47.281133Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-577c00","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pipeline stage 4: Mesh — extract triangles from visible volumes","description":"Define the Mesh stage interface. Takes visible volume cells and extracts triangle meshes (vertices + indices + colors/normals). Initial implementation: emit one quad per visible voxel face (voxel adjacent to air).\n\n### Deliverables\n- `MeshOutput` type: vertex buffer data, index buffer data, vertex count\n- `MeshExtractor` trait with `extract(volume, visibility) -\u003e MeshOutput`\n- Simple face extractor: for each non-air voxel with an air neighbor, emit a colored quad\n- Wired into Engine::render_frame between cull and upload stages","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a4","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-577c00","target_id":"sw-59c80a","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","meshing","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:02:57.905197Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-dcc28a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pipeline stage 5: Upload — stage mesh data to GPU","description":"Define the Upload stage. Takes CPU-side mesh data and creates/updates GPU buffers (vertex, index). Initial implementation: create_buffer with mapped_at_creation (simple, synchronous). The ring buffer and async copy queue come later.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `GpuMesh` type: wgpu vertex buffer, index buffer, index count\n- Upload stage converts MeshOutput → GpuMesh\n- Engine caches GpuMesh, only re-uploads when mesh data changes\n- Wired into Engine::render_frame between mesh and execute stages","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a5","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-dcc28a","target_id":"sw-577c00","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","streaming","gpu-transfer","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:03:07.463566Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-49724f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Pipeline stage 6: Execute — rasterize and present","description":"Define the Execute stage. Takes GPU meshes and the view, rasterizes via vertex/fragment pipeline, presents to surface. Replaces the placeholder cube renderer with a real voxel rasterizer.\n\n### Deliverables\n- Vertex/fragment shader for colored voxel faces (position + normal + color)\n- Render pipeline with depth testing\n- Execute stage draws all GpuMesh entries with the current ViewState\n- Wired into Engine::render_frame as the final stage\n- Placeholder renderer removed\n- Sandbox shows terrain","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":5,"sort_order":"a6","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-49724f","target_id":"sw-dcc28a","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","rasterization","rendering","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:03:17.15682Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-fb5789","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## OOC Pipeline: End-to-End Skeleton\n\nWire up the full OOC pipeline with concrete types flowing between stages. Each stage has a real interface; initial implementations are no-op/passthrough where the real algorithm comes later. The pipeline runs every frame inside Engine::render_frame.\n\n### Pipeline (top level)\n\n```\nGame: worldgen on job pool → populate World (volumes + lights + entities)\n\nEngine: Cull → Stream → Execute\n                          ├── HZB build\n                          ├── Depth prepass\n                          ├── Shadow atlas\n                          ├── GBuffer / base pass\n                          ├── Light grid (clustered)\n                          ├── Shade (deferred lighting)\n                          ├── Screen-space FX (SSAO, SSR)\n                          ├── Transparency\n                          ├── Post-process (tone map, TAA, bloom)\n                          └── Present\n```\n\n### Key corrections from engine research\n\n1. **Meshing is async, not per-frame** — triggered by visibility changes, runs on worker threads, cached. Current frame renders cached meshes. This matches how Unity/Unreal/Godot handle geometry.\n2. **Execute is a sub-pipeline** — not a single draw call. All major engines decompose rendering into 8-10 sub-passes.\n3. **Lighting infrastructure from day one** — light lists, clustered shading, shadow atlas. Games may have dozens of lights.\n4. **Post-processing is not optional** — tone mapping required for HDR→display, TAA critical for voxel edge aliasing.\n\n### Goal\n\nData flows end-to-end. Every stage has the right interface. No-op implementations where real algorithms come later, but the types and data flow are production-ready. Designed for what games need, not what the sandbox currently uses.\n\n### Dependencies\n- Depends on E1 for Engine, World, VoxelVolume, JobPool\""},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:01:27.19795Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-2985d8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"World accepts volumes and lights","description":"World becomes the container for everything the engine renders: volumes, lights, and entities. Games populate it; the engine reads it.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `World::add_volume()` — store VoxelVolume trait objects\n- `World::add_light()` — store light descriptors (directional, point, spot with position, color, intensity, range, shadow-casting flag)\n- `Light` enum/struct covering all light types the engine supports\n- Adding/removing volumes or lights marks World dirty\n- Engine's render_frame reads volumes and lights from World\n\n### Design note\nThe light data structure must support what games need: a sun, dozens of torches, spot lights, emissive sources. Not just what the sandbox uses today.\"","labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","world","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:01:46.321197Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-7fe21e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Cull stage: frustum + visibility determination","description":"Top-level pipeline stage. Takes World (volumes, lights, entities) + ViewState, produces a VisibilitySet — what needs rendering this frame. Initial implementation: everything visible (passthrough). Interface ready for frustum culling, HZB occlusion, SSE evaluation.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `VisibilitySet` type: visible volume cells, visible lights, visible entities\n- `CullStage` trait or struct with `cull(world, view) -\u003e VisibilitySet`\n- No-op implementation: marks everything visible\n- Wired into Engine::render_frame as the first stage\n- Interface accepts AABB buffer + HZB texture for future GPU culling\"","dependencies":[{"source_id":"","target_id":"sw-2985d8","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","culling","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:01:58.63971Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-59c80a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Stream stage: async mesh + upload pipeline","description":"Top-level pipeline stage. Cull results trigger async work: meshing volumes that became visible, evicting meshes that left view. Runs on the engine's job pool. The current frame renders whatever's already cached — streaming never blocks the frame.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `MeshCache` — maps volume cell IDs to cached `GpuMesh` (vertex + index buffers)\n- `StreamStage` receives VisibilitySet, submits mesh jobs for uncached visible cells\n- `MeshExtractor` trait: `extract(volume_cell) -\u003e MeshData` (CPU-side vertices + indices)\n- Simple face extractor: one quad per visible voxel face (voxel adjacent to air)\n- Upload: `MeshData` → `GpuMesh` (create_buffer with mapped_at_creation)\n- Job pool drains completed meshes each frame, inserts into cache\n- Eviction: meshes for cells no longer visible are freed after N frames\n\n### Key design point\nMeshing is async and cached. A newly visible cell renders at coarse LOD (or not at all) until its mesh job completes. This matches how all major engines handle geometry — pre-meshed, cached, streamed on demand.\"","estimate":8,"dependencies":[{"source_id":"","target_id":"sw-7fe21e","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","streaming","meshing","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:02:13.393524Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-577c00","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Execute sub-pipeline: depth prepass + GBuffer + HZB","description":"First sub-stages of Execute. Render visible cached meshes into a GBuffer (position, albedo, normal, material) with depth. Build the HZB mip chain from depth for next frame's occlusion culling.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `GBuffer` struct: depth (Depth32Float), position (Rgba32Float), albedo (Rgba8Unorm), normal (Rgba8Snorm), material/roughness/metallic (Rgba8Unorm)\n- Vertex/fragment shader for voxel faces: writes all GBuffer targets\n- Depth prepass (optional, can fuse with GBuffer pass initially)\n- `HZBBuilder`: compute shader that downsamples depth into a mip chain (power-of-two, max per 2x2)\n- HZB output stored for next frame's Cull stage\n- Replaces placeholder cube renderer\n\n### Design note\nGBuffer format must support PBR materials (roughness, metallic) from day one — games will have different materials (stone, wood, metal, water surface).\"","dependencies":[{"source_id":"","target_id":"sw-59c80a","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","rendering","gbuffer","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:02:27.117132Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-dcc28a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Execute sub-pipeline: shadow atlas + light grid + deferred shade","description":"Lighting sub-stages of Execute. Build shadow maps for shadow-casting lights, construct a clustered light grid, evaluate all lights against the GBuffer in a deferred shading pass.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `LightBuffer` — GPU SSBO of light structs (type, position, direction, color, intensity, range, shadow atlas index)\n- Shadow atlas: depth-only render per shadow-casting light (cascaded for directional, single map for spot, cube/dual-paraboloid for point)\n- Initial: single cascade for one directional light, interface supports N lights\n- `ClusteredLightGrid` — 3D grid (screen tiles × depth slices), each cell lists affecting lights\n- Deferred shade pass: compute or fragment shader reads GBuffer + light grid + shadow atlas, outputs HDR color\n- Supports directional, point, spot lights — not just a hardcoded sun\n\n### Design note\nThe light grid must scale to dozens of lights. A game with torches in a dungeon, campfires, magical effects, and a sun needs clustered shading from day one.\"","estimate":8,"dependencies":[{"source_id":"","target_id":"sw-577c00","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","rendering","lighting","shadows","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:02:43.87741Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-49724f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Execute sub-pipeline: screen FX + transparency + post-process + present","description":"Final sub-stages of Execute. Screen-space effects, transparent geometry, post-processing stack, and presentation.\n\n### Deliverables\n- **SSAO**: screen-space ambient occlusion from depth + normals. Compute shader, half-res, bilateral blur. Initial: simple SSAO, interface for GTAO/HBAO later.\n- **SSR**: screen-space reflections. Ray march in screen space against HZB. Initial: no-op, interface ready.\n- **Transparency pass**: forward-lit transparent geometry sorted back-to-front. Initial: no-op (voxels are opaque), interface ready for water, particles, glass.\n- **Post-processing stack**: ordered list of full-screen passes:\n  - Tone mapping (ACES or similar, HDR → display LDR) — required from day one\n  - TAA (temporal anti-aliasing) — critical for voxel edge aliasing\n  - Bloom — threshold + downsample + upsample blur chain\n  - Depth of field — initial: no-op\n  - Motion blur — initial: no-op\n- **Present**: blit final color to swapchain surface\n\n### Design note\nPost-processing is not polish — tone mapping is required to display HDR lighting correctly, TAA is required to hide voxel staircase aliasing and LOD transition shimmer.\"","estimate":8,"dependencies":[{"source_id":"","target_id":"sw-dcc28a","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","rendering","post-process","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:02:58.941629Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
