{"id":"sw-2985d8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1e72b017-6cf9-447f-b23f-8a84d5651e71","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — World is now the hybrid scene container with five collections:\n\n- `light.rs` — `LightKind` enum (Directional/Point/Spot) + `Light` struct with convenience constructors\n- `material.rs` — `Material` struct (PBR scalars: base_color, roughness, metallic, emissive)\n- `mesh.rs` — `Vertex` (PBR vertex format), `Mesh` (shared geometry asset with auto-computed AABB), `MeshInstance` (placed object referencing `MeshKey` + `MaterialKey`)\n- `world.rs` — Complete rewrite. `World` holds `SlotMap` collections for volumes, meshes, mesh instances, materials, and lights. Per-object `ChangeSet\u003cK\u003e` tracks spawned/despawned/mutated keys. `drain_changes()` returns a `WorldChanges` struct consumed by pipeline stages.\n- `engine.rs` — `render_frame` calls `world.drain_changes()` instead of the old `WorldGpuData::extract`\n\n`VoxelModel` and `VoxelInstance` removed from World. `WorldGpuData::extract` stubbed until pipeline stages land.\n\n**Rationale** — Hybrid architecture (voxel volumes + mesh instances + shared materials + lights) matches UE5/Unity/Godot. Per-object change tracking matches UE5's `MarkRenderStateDirty` / Godot's per-instance dirty list. Lights excluded from tracking — re-packed every frame. Materials shared via `MaterialKey` reference, not embedded per-instance.\n\n**Decisions made**\n- `Mesh` + `MeshInstance` naming (follows Godot convention)\n- `Light::directional()` enables shadows by default; point/spot disable them\n- `Mesh::new()` auto-computes AABB from vertices\n- `#[allow(dead_code)]` on `DrainedChanges`, `WorldChanges`, `WorldGpuData::extract` — consumed by pipeline stages in subsequent issues\n\n**Status** — 61 tests passing, clippy clean, ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T21:49:45.466871Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-8d894c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Material texture maps (albedo, normal, roughness/metallic)","description":"## Material Texture Support\n\nExtend `Material` from scalar-only PBR properties to support texture maps. Games need textured surfaces — stone walls, wooden floors, metal armor all require per-texel variation that scalar values can't express.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- **Texture asset type** — `Texture` struct (image data, format, dimensions, mip levels) stored in World via `TextureKey`\n- **Material gains texture slots** — `Material` fields for albedo map, normal map, roughness/metallic map, emissive map (all `Option\u003cTextureKey\u003e`)\n- **GPU texture array or bindless** — upload textures to GPU, make them available in the GBuffer shader\n- **Sampler configuration** — filtering (bilinear/trilinear/aniso), wrap mode, per-texture or per-material\n- **Fallback to scalar** — when no texture is bound, the existing scalar values (`base_color`, `roughness`, `metallic`, `emissive`) are used as-is. Textures multiply with or replace scalars (standard PBR convention).\n\n### Design considerations\n\n- Texture memory management (streaming, residency, virtual texturing) is separate from basic texture support\n- Normal maps require tangent-space lighting in the GBuffer shader — the `Vertex` format already has tangents\n- Roughness and metallic are often packed into one texture (ORM map: occlusion + roughness + metallic) — the Material struct should support both split and packed formats\n\n### Dependencies\n- Depends on GBuffer (sw-577c00) for the shader side — textures need to be sampled in the GBuffer fragment/compute pass","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":8,"sort_order":"b15","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-8d894c","target_id":"sw-577c00","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","engine","materials","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T21:50:26.688983Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
