{"id":"sw-7fe21e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9224644b-d7b8-4375-ba31-3ddd1693ec37","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — `cull.rs` adds `VisibilitySet` (visible volume/mesh instance/light keys) and `CullStage` with a no-op passthrough that marks everything visible. Wired into `Engine::render_frame` after `drain_changes()`.\n\n**Rationale** — establishes the World → Cull → VisibilitySet data flow. No-op is correct for the skeleton; the interface accepts `\u0026ViewState` + optional HZB texture so real culling can replace the body without changing the signature.\n\n**Decisions made** — struct over trait (no polymorphism needed), Vec over HashSet (linear iteration, cache-friendly), `#[derive(Default)]` per clippy.\n\n**Status** — 64 tests passing, clippy clean, ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:00:12.482938Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
