{"id":"sw-f53904","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-f53904","target_id":"sw-59c80a"}],"description":"## GPU Buffer Pooling\n\nReplace per-volume/per-mesh individual `wgpu::Buffer` allocations with a slab allocator that suballocates from a few large GPU buffers.\n\n### Why\n\nEach `device.create_buffer` call has overhead (Vulkan memory allocation, descriptor updates). UE5 suballocates from a single large streaming pool. As volume/mesh count grows, per-object allocation becomes a bottleneck and fragments GPU memory.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Slab allocator or ring buffer for GPU vertex/index data\n- Allocate large buffers up front, suballocate regions for individual meshes\n- Free-list tracking with coalescing\n- Eviction returns region to free-list instead of destroying buffer\n- Integration with StreamStage's MeshCache\n\n### Design considerations\n\n- Variable-size allocations (different volumes produce different mesh sizes)\n- Fragmentation strategy (best-fit, first-fit, buddy allocator)\n- Growth policy when pool is exhausted\n- Alignment requirements for vertex/index data","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","streaming","optimization"],"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","sort_order":"b16","status":"BACKLOG","title":"GPU buffer pooling / suballocation for mesh streaming"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:16:44.17542Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
