{"id":"sw-c162ed","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-c162ed","target_id":"sw-59c80a"}],"description":"## Pipeline Profiling \u0026 Instrumentation\n\nWire up profiling infrastructure so every pipeline stage reports timing and resource usage. Gated behind a debug flag — zero overhead when disabled.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- **CPU stage timers** — wall-clock time for each top-level stage (Cull, Stream, Execute) and Execute sub-stages. Use `Instant::now()` pairs, stored as EMA-smoothed averages matching `GpuTimestamps` style.\n- **GPU timestamps** — wire existing `GpuTimestamps` into the Execute sub-pipeline passes (depth prepass, GBuffer, shadow, shade, post-process). The infrastructure exists in `gpu_timing.rs` but is unused by the new pipeline.\n- **Memory stats** — `MeshCache` total bytes, volume mesh count, mesh asset count, pending job count, ready queue depth. Already partially exposed via `MeshCache` accessors.\n- **Debug output** — periodic log output (every N frames) with stage timings and memory stats when `EngineConfig` debug flag is set. Future: on-screen overlay via egui or similar.\n- **Per-frame stats struct** — `FrameStats` collecting all metrics in one place, accessible to games for custom display.\n\n### Design note\n\nThis should be zero-cost when disabled. Use a compile-time feature flag or a runtime bool that the compiler can branch-predict away. Don't add timing calls that survive in release builds.\n\n### Dependencies\n\n- Depends on Execute sub-pipeline stages existing (sw-577c00, sw-dcc28a, sw-49724f) for GPU timestamp wiring\n- CPU stage timers and memory stats can land as soon as Cull + Stream exist (now)","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","profiling","phase-1"],"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","sort_order":"b15","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Pipeline profiling: CPU stage timers, GPU timestamps, memory stats"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:29:59.33593Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
