{"id":"sw-59c80a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0e64e145-b51d-469b-95e5-5543e58850ce","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — `stream.rs` adds the full async mesh extraction + GPU upload pipeline: `MeshExtractor` trait with `PlaceholderExtractor`, `MeshCache` with priority-based eviction (256 MB budget), `StreamStage` with per-frame upload budget (8 MB), priority ordering (closest first), ready queue, and pending dedup. Wired into `Engine::render_frame` after cull. Research reports saved to `docs/research/`.\n\n**Rationale** — Design informed by UE5/Unity/Godot research. Upload budget prevents frame spikes (Unity pattern). Priority eviction replaces naive frame-count (UE5 pattern). Never blocks the frame (UE5 pattern).\n\n**Decisions made** — `Arc\u003cdyn MeshExtractor\u003e` for safe job submission, `pub(crate)` on `stream()` to avoid exposing internal types, 8 MB upload / 256 MB cache defaults.\n\n**Status** — 73 tests passing, clippy clean, user approved."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:32:11.603069Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
