{"id":"sw-117099","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-117099","target_id":"sw-577c00"}],"description":"## Instanced \u0026 Indirect Drawing\n\nReplace per-draw uniform writes + individual draw calls with instanced drawing (batching objects sharing the same mesh) and GPU-driven indirect dispatch.\n\n### Why\n\nThe skeleton GBuffer pass writes uniforms and issues a draw call per object. At scale (hundreds/thousands of objects), this becomes CPU-bound: uniform buffer writes, draw call overhead, and pipeline state changes dominate. Instanced drawing batches objects sharing the same mesh into a single draw call. Indirect dispatch lets the GPU drive the draw count from the Cull stage output, eliminating CPU readback.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- **Instance buffer** — per-instance data (model matrix, material properties) packed into a GPU storage buffer. Indexed by `gl_InstanceIndex` in the vertex shader.\n- **Instanced draw** — one `draw_indexed_indirect` per unique mesh, with instance count from the visible set. Objects sharing a `MeshKey` are batched.\n- **Indirect draw buffer** — GPU-written draw commands from the Cull stage (future: GPU culling writes the indirect buffer directly, zero CPU involvement).\n- **Material buffer** — SSBO of material properties indexed by material ID, replacing per-draw uniform writes.\n\n### Design considerations\n\n- Instancing groups by MeshKey. Objects with the same mesh but different materials still batch — material is looked up per-instance from the material SSBO.\n- Indirect dispatch pairs naturally with GPU frustum/occlusion culling — the GPU writes the draw commands.\n- Instance data update should be incremental (per-object change tracking from World already exists).","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","optimization"],"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","sort_order":"b15","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Instanced / indirect draw for mesh rendering"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:37:14.531849Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-577c00","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:40:12.628497Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-4957d0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-4957d0","target_id":"sw-577c00"},{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-4957d0","target_id":"sw-8d894c"}],"description":"## Depth Prepass\n\nAdd a separate depth-only render pass before the GBuffer pass. The GBuffer fragment shader then runs with early-Z rejection, skipping overdraw entirely.\n\n### Why\n\nThe fused GBuffer pass (sw-577c00) has no depth prepass because the initial fragment shader writes constants — zero overdraw cost. Once fragment shaders become expensive (texture sampling from sw-8d894c, complex BRDF, parallax mapping), overdraw becomes a real cost. A depth prepass renders all geometry depth-only first, then the GBuffer pass runs with `depth_compare: Equal` so every fragment is shaded exactly once.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Depth-only render pass (vertex shader only, no fragment output)\n- GBuffer pass uses `depth_compare: Equal`, `depth_write: false`\n- Toggle via `EngineConfig` flag (scenes with low overdraw skip the prepass)\n- Benchmark comparison: with/without prepass at various scene complexities\n\n### When to add\n\nWhen fragment shader cost justifies the extra geometry pass. Indicators:\n- Texture sampling in the GBuffer shader (sw-8d894c)\n- Complex material evaluation (parallax, detail maps)\n- High overdraw ratio (dense scenes, lots of overlapping geometry)","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","optimization"],"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","sort_order":"b16","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Depth prepass for overdraw reduction"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T22:42:45.643496Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
