{"id":"sw-76487b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"sw-76487b","target_id":"sw-577c00"}],"description":"## HZB Mip Chain Build\n\nWire up the compute shader that downsamples the depth buffer into the HZB mip chain. The HZB texture is already allocated (sw-577c00), but the actual mip chain build is deferred because Depth32Float cannot be reinterpreted as R32Float directly in wgpu.\n\n### Why\n\nThe HZB mip chain enables GPU occlusion culling in the Cull stage — project AABBs to screen space and test against the mip chain to reject fully occluded geometry without rasterization.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Depth → R32Float copy pass (compute shader reading `texture_depth_2d`, writing to HZB mip 0)\n- Mip chain downsample (compute shader reading R32Float mip N-1, writing mip N with max of 2x2 block)\n- Wire HZB output into CullStage as `Some(\u0026hzb_view)`\n- The `hzb.wgsl` shader already exists — needs a variant for the depth texture input\n\n### Technical note\n\nwgpu does not support creating a R32Float view of a Depth32Float texture. The first mip requires a separate compute pass that reads from `texture_depth_2d` and writes to `texture_storage_2d\u003cr32float\u003e`. Subsequent mips use the existing `hzb.wgsl` which reads `texture_2d\u003cf32\u003e`.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","ooc-pipeline","culling","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","sort_order":"b15","status":"BACKLOG","title":"HZB mip chain build (depth downsampling compute pass)"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T23:03:18.60313Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-577c00","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"walkthrough","filename":"walkthrough.md"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T07:38:03.544385Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-577c00","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-55e3b509-0875-4e62-b394-a85aef800001","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — GBuffer pass replaces placeholder renderer. `gbuffer.wgsl` writes albedo (Rgba8UnormSrgb), octahedral normals (Rgba8Unorm), material (Rgba8Unorm) with Depth32Float. Debug blit shows flat albedo on screen. HZB texture allocated, build deferred (sw-76487b). Position reconstructed from depth (no explicit position buffer).\n\n**Rationale** — depth reconstruction saves 33 MB. Octahedral normals halve normal storage. Dynamic uniform buffer offsets for per-draw data. MRT fused pass maximizes tile GPU efficiency.\n\n**Decisions made** — fixed sandbox floor winding (backface culling), `#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` on render(), HZB build deferred due to Depth32Float→R32Float limitation in wgpu.\n\n**Status** — 73 tests passing, clippy clean, visual validation confirmed (flat stone-colored floor quad visible). User approved."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T07:38:14.233618Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.222 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
