{"id":"sw-0dd1c0","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"parent_id":"sw-713dd5"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:48:49.474626Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-419f19","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-419f19","target_id":"sw-2985d8"}],"description":"## Skinned Meshes\n\nAdd bone weights, skeleton hierarchy, and GPU skinning to the mesh pipeline. `MeshInstance` currently supports static and rigid-body meshes only.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- `SkinnedVertex` with bone indices + weights (4 bones per vertex)\n- `Skeleton` struct: joint hierarchy with bind-pose inverse matrices\n- `AnimationClip`: keyframed joint transforms (position, rotation, scale)\n- GPU skinning compute pass: transforms vertices by bone matrices before GBuffer pass\n- `SkinnedMeshInstance` in World with skeleton + active animation state\n\n### Design note\n\nDiscovered during sw-2985d8 (hybrid World). Current `Vertex` and `MeshInstance` are static-only. Skinned meshes are required for creatures, characters, and animated props.","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","engine","rendering","animation"],"parent_id":"sw-713dd5","sort_order":"b1A","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Skinned mesh support (bone weights, skeleton, animation)"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:48:57.288077Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-106f56","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-106f56","target_id":"sw-314e8f"}],"description":"## Incremental Extract\n\nReplace full-rebuild extraction with per-instance generation comparison and partial buffer updates via `write_buffer` offsets. Currently the extraction boundary rebuilds all GPU buffers when anything changes.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Per-instance generation counter compared against last-extracted generation\n- Partial buffer updates: only write changed instances via `write_buffer` offset\n- Skip extraction entirely when no instances changed\n- Benchmark: full rebuild vs incremental at 100, 1000, 10000 instances\n\n### Origin\n\nDiscovered during sw-314e8f (World struct introduction). The mechanism is in place (generation counter exists) but incremental path was deferred.","estimate":3,"labels":["optimization","engine","rendering"],"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","sort_order":"b1B","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Incremental World extract with per-instance generation tracking"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:04.393511Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-621977","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-621977","target_id":"sw-de79da"}],"description":"## Fullscreen Support\n\nImplement the `WindowMode::Fullscreen` variant. Currently the enum variant exists but `Engine::new` falls back to 1920×1080 windowed. Needs proper exclusive fullscreen or borderless windowed fullscreen via winit.\n\n### Origin\n\nDiscovered during sw-de79da (Engine struct). Variant declared, not implemented.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","engine","api"],"sort_order":"b1C","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Fullscreen window mode"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:07.217566Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3360a6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-3360a6","target_id":"sw-217282"}],"description":"## Configurable Escape Key\n\nEngine currently hardcodes Escape → quit in the event handler. Games need to override this (e.g., Escape → pause menu). Move escape handling from engine internals to a configurable callback or let games consume it via the input snapshot.\n\n### Origin\n\nDiscovered during sw-217282 (Input snapshot). Escape is infrastructure today but games will want to override it.","estimate":1,"labels":["feature","engine","input","api"],"sort_order":"b1D","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Configurable escape key behavior"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:10.798032Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-ccfce7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-ccfce7","target_id":"sw-217282"}],"description":"## Action Mapping\n\nAdd an action mapping layer on top of the raw input snapshot. Games bind named actions (\"jump\", \"attack\", \"interact\") to keys/buttons, then query `input.action_pressed(\"jump\")` instead of `input.key_pressed(KeyCode::Space)`. Supports rebinding, multiple bindings per action, and gamepad + keyboard unified.\n\n### Origin\n\nDiscovered during sw-217282 (Input snapshot). Raw key queries are the foundation this sits on.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","engine","input"],"sort_order":"b1E","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Input action mapping system"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:14.293761Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-a93f4d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-a93f4d","target_id":"sw-b87f8e"}],"description":"## Priority Queues for Job Pool\n\nReplace the single FIFO queue in `JobPool` with priority queues. High-priority jobs (visible chunk meshing) should preempt low-priority work (prefetching distant chunks). Work-stealing between workers to avoid idle threads.\n\n### Origin\n\nDiscovered during sw-b87f8e (persistent worker pool). Single FIFO was the initial implementation.","estimate":3,"labels":["optimization","engine","jobs","concurrency"],"parent_id":"sw-2c3e44","sort_order":"b1F","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Job pool priority queues with work-stealing"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:18.595876Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-106f56","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:21.011602Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"sw-ca642a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"sw-ca642a","target_id":"sw-dcc28a"}],"description":"## Light Culling\n\nThe CullStage includes all lights in the VisibilitySet (no-op passthrough). Point and spot lights that are entirely off-screen should be culled before they reach the light buffer and cluster assignment. Directional lights are always included.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Sphere-frustum test for point lights (position + range)\n- Cone-frustum test for spot lights (or bounding sphere approximation)\n- Directional lights bypass culling\n- Benchmark: culling 100 point lights, verify off-screen ones are excluded\n\n### Origin\n\nDiscovered during sw-7fe21e (Cull stage). Lights are in the VisibilitySet but not actually culled.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","engine","culling","lighting"],"parent_id":"sw-2e26ca","sort_order":"b1G","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Point/spot light frustum culling in CullStage"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:49:24.595576Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-621977","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"parent_id":"sw-fb5789","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:50:27.280718Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-e1e582","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Advanced Input System\n\nInput improvements beyond the basic frame-snapshot polling (sw-217282). Covers action mapping, configurable key behavior, gamepad support, and input rebinding.\n\n### Relationship to E1.5\n\nE1.5 delivered the raw input snapshot — keyboard held/pressed/released, mouse position/delta/buttons. This epic builds higher-level abstractions on that foundation: named actions, rebindable keys, and giving games control over engine-level key handling.","estimate":5,"labels":["epic","engine","input"],"sort_order":"b1H","status":"BACKLOG","title":"E8: Advanced Input System"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T08:50:22.92845Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
