{"id":"sw-7dd08f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"awV"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T11:40:04.539731Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"sw-8a89c4","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Scripting Runtime\n\nEmbedded Lua scripting for game rules, AI behaviors, and mod support via `mlua`.\n\n### Decision: Lua via mlua\n\nLua wins over Rhai for this engine:\n\n- **Performance** — LuaJIT is 2-5× of C for tight loops; Rhai is significantly slower\n- **Ecosystem** — massive gamedev community, decades of AAA track record (CryEngine, Roblox, Factorio, WoW)\n- **Accessibility** — designers and modders can pick it up without being Rust/C++ engineers\n- **mlua** — mature Rust crate with proper lifetime safety, async support, and Lua 5.4 / LuaJIT backends\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Lua runtime via mlua** — embed Lua 5.4 (or LuaJIT) with `mlua`, sandboxed per-script\n- **Engine API bindings** — spawn/despawn entities, query voxels, edit bricks, play sounds, show UI, read input\n- **Script execution** — scripts run in job system workers, sandboxed, with per-frame budget (instruction count limit)\n- **Hot reload** — watch script files, reload on change without restart\n- **Event hooks** — on_tick, on_collide, on_interact, on_damage, etc.\n\n### Non-goals (game crate territory)\n\n- Specific game scripts (monster AI, crafting rules, quest logic)\n- Script asset organization and loading order"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T11:41:15.367925Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.225 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-3d9d06","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Lua runtime integration via mlua: sandboxed execution with per-frame budget","description":"## Lua Runtime Integration\n\nEmbed Lua 5.4 (with LuaJIT as optional backend) using `mlua`.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Add `mlua` dependency with `lua54` and `vendored` features\n- Create `ScriptRuntime` struct owning `mlua::Lua` instance\n- Sandbox: disable `os`, `io`, `debug` modules; whitelist safe stdlib\n- Per-frame instruction budget via `set_hook` (count-based limit to prevent infinite loops)\n- Script loading from file path or string\n- Error handling: capture Lua errors, surface as `ScriptError` with source location\n- Hot reload: file watcher triggers script re-evaluation without engine restart\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `mlua` compiles and links with vendored Lua 5.4\n- [ ] `ScriptRuntime::new()` creates a sandboxed Lua state\n- [ ] Scripts exceeding instruction budget are terminated gracefully\n- [ ] `os.execute`, `io.open`, `loadfile` are blocked in sandbox\n- [ ] Hot reload detects file changes and reloads without restart\n- [ ] Unit tests for sandbox enforcement and budget limits"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T11:41:22.486955Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.225 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"sw-70f1e1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## C FFI Layer (`crates/smallworld-ffi`)\n\nThin `extern \"C\"` wrapper crate exposing the engine API to C, C++, and any language with C interop.\n\n### Motivation\n\nGames don't have to be written in Rust. A stable C ABI lets C++ studios, C# (via P/Invoke), Python (via ctypes/cffi), and other languages use the engine. This is the standard approach — Unity (C++ core, C# games), Godot (C++ core, GDScript/C# games), Unreal (C++ with reflection).\n\n### Scope\n\n- **Crate scaffold** — `crates/smallworld-ffi` as a `cdylib` crate\n- **Opaque handle pattern** — engine objects exposed as `*mut c_void` handles with create/destroy pairs\n- **Core API surface** — engine init/shutdown, window creation, frame loop, entity spawn/despawn\n- **C header generation** — use `cbindgen` to auto-generate `smallworld.h` from Rust source\n- **Error handling** — thread-local last-error with `sw_get_last_error()` (no panics across FFI)\n- **ABI stability** — versioned API with `sw_version()` check\n\n### Non-goals (for now)\n\n- Full engine API coverage (start with core loop + entities, expand later)\n- Language-specific bindings (C#, Python wrappers are separate stories)\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `crates/smallworld-ffi` builds as `libsmallworld.dylib` / `.so` / `.dll`\n- [ ] `cbindgen` generates valid `smallworld.h`\n- [ ] A minimal C program can link against the dylib, create a window, and run the frame loop\n- [ ] No Rust panics cross the FFI boundary (catch_unwind at every entry point)\n- [ ] `sw_version()` returns the crate version","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","engine","ffi"],"parent_id":"sw-ef7223","sort_order":"b1H","status":"BACKLOG","title":"C FFI layer: expose engine API for C/C++ consumers"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T11:41:34.913416Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.225 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
