{"id":"sw-dcc28a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ed5d2494-a719-43d2-b754-a4a2e25c0e6c","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — Full deferred lighting pipeline added. `lighting.rs` implements `LightBuffer` (SSBO packing for 256 lights), `ShadowAtlas` (4096² Depth32Float with grid subdivision), `ClusteredLightGrid` (CPU-side assignment, 80px tiles, 24 logarithmic depth slices with clamped near-plane), and `LightingPass` (shade compute dispatch + Reinhard HDR blit). Two new shaders: `shadow.wgsl` (depth-only vertex shader with front-face culling + slope bias) and `shade.wgsl` (full Cook-Torrance PBR compute shader with GGX distribution, Smith-GGX geometry, Schlick fresnel, UE4-style smooth attenuation, shadow atlas sampling, and clustered light lookup). `blit.wgsl` updated with Reinhard tone mapping. Debug albedo blit removed from `GBufferPass`. Pipeline flow is now `gbuffer → shadow → shade → blit_hdr → present`.\n\n**Rationale** — Compute shader for shade pass confirmed by research (Unity HDRP uses compute, UE5 auto-switches at \u003e80 lights). 4096² atlas matches Unity HDRP and Godot 4 defaults. Logarithmic cluster depth with `max(near, 0.5)` clamp avoids near-plane singularity (Doom 2016 approach). Reinhard provides a reasonable HDR preview until proper tone mapping lands (sw-49724f).\n\n**Decisions made** — Atlas subdivision uses simple grid packing (`sqrt(N)` subdivision) rather than Godot's quadrant system. Shadow comparison sampler with `LessEqual` for correct shadow test direction. `GBuffer` fields exposed via `gbuffer()` accessor rather than making struct fields public. Blit shader applies Reinhard globally (per-channel `c / (c + 1)`) rather than luminance-based.\n\n**Status** — 81 tests passing (8 new), clippy clean, ready for visual review."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T11:45:18.458865Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
