{"id":"sw-72e0e0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"GLB/glTF mesh import","description":"## GLB/glTF Mesh Import\n\nAdd a loader that reads `.glb` / `.gltf` files and produces `Mesh`, `Material`, and `MeshInstance` entries in the World. This is the engine's first file-based asset path and proves the hybrid mesh pipeline works with real content, not just procedural geometry.\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- `assets::load_glb(path) -\u003e LoadedScene` — reads a GLB file, returns meshes, materials, and a scene graph of instances\n- `LoadedScene::spawn(world) -\u003e Vec\u003cMeshInstanceKey\u003e` — convenience to add everything to a World\n- Maps glTF PBR material properties to our `Material` struct (baseColorFactor → base_color, roughnessFactor, metallicFactor)\n- Vertex format: position, normal, UV, tangent (matches our `Vertex` layout)\n- Handles multi-mesh scenes (a GLB can contain many meshes + a node tree)\n- Sandbox updated to load a GLB file from a path (CLI arg or hardcoded test asset)\n\n### Non-goals (future)\n\n- Texture maps (albedo, normal, roughness/metallic) — scalar material properties only for now (sw-8d894c)\n- Skinned meshes / animations (sw-419f19)\n- Async loading / streaming\n\n### Why glTF\n\n- Standard interchange format (Khronos)\n- PBR material model maps directly to our Material struct\n- Binary variant (GLB) is self-contained (geometry + materials in one file)\n- Rust `gltf` crate is mature and well-maintained\n- Every 3D tool exports it (Blender, Sketchfab, etc.)\n\n### Dependency\n\nNew crate dependency: `gltf` (MIT licensed)","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"sw-fb5789","estimate":3,"sort_order":"b1G","dependencies":[{"source_id":"sw-72e0e0","target_id":"sw-dcc28a","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","engine","assets","phase-1"]},"created_at":"2026-08-08T12:01:32.016946Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
