{"id":"sw-72e0e0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b4617f73-fe06-41cb-bf8e-7f06892979bf","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — `load_glb()` in `assets.rs` reads GLB/glTF files via the `gltf` crate. Maps vertex attributes (position, normal, UV, tangent) to engine `Vertex`, PBR scalar properties to `Material`, and flattens the node tree into `MeshInstance`s with world transforms. `double_sided` flag added to `MeshInstance` with two GBuffer pipeline variants (culled / no-cull) and `@builtin(front_facing)` normal flip. Sandbox accepts `cargo run -- path/to/model.glb`.\n\n**Rationale** — glTF is the standard interchange format with a PBR material model that maps 1:1 to our `Material` struct. The `gltf` crate handles all binary parsing.\n\n**Decisions made** — `double_sided` lives on `MeshInstance` (not `Material`) since it's a rendering decision per-instance. Texture maps deferred to sw-8d894c (moved back to E1.5).\n\n**Status** — Tested with Sketchfab model, geometry and materials render correctly. Clippy issues are from concurrent rayon migration, not this change."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T12:38:56.078945Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
