{"id":"sw-e475fe","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2835ad11-02e5-41cd-b01e-c5c7df5385fa","text":"**Summary:** Replaced `JobPool` with a two-layer job system: `Scheduler` trait + `RayonScheduler` backend. `TaskHandle\u003cT\u003e` provides typed spawn/wait/poll. StreamStage migrated from type-erased `Box\u003cdyn Any\u003e` drain to typed handles with `HashSet` + `Vec\u003cTaskHandle\u003e` (Option C).\n\n**Rationale:** Two-layer design (from UE5 research) lets us swap rayon for a custom crossbeam-deque scheduler later without touching callers. Typed handles eliminate the `downcast` failure path.\n\n**Decisions made:** Used `Mutex\u003cOption\u003cT\u003e\u003e` for TaskHandle cache instead of `UnsafeCell` — workspace denies `unsafe_code`, and the uncontended lock cost is negligible. Thread count set to `cores - 4` (reserving main + GPU + audio + headroom).\n\n**Status:** 85 tests passing, clippy clean, user tophatted — sandbox boots and renders with streaming functional."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T12:42:16.5853Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.225 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
