{"id":"sw-8d894c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d45ea9b6-7ba7-47dd-bb7f-50711b762bdc","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n**Summary** — `TextureData` + `TextureKey` in World. `Material` gains `albedo_map`, `normal_map`, `roughness_metallic_map` (all `Option\u003cTextureKey\u003e`). GBufferPass has GPU texture cache with lazy upload, 1×1 fallback textures, and per-draw texture bind group (group 2). GBuffer shader samples all three textures with TBN normal mapping via vertex tangents. GLB loader reads embedded glTF images (RGBA8 conversion), maps texture references to `MaterialTextures` indices. Sandbox GLB scene updated with three-point lighting.\n\n**Rationale** — Without textures, GLB models render as flat white. The fallback texture design means the shader always samples unconditionally — no branching, materials without textures get identity values that preserve scalar properties.\n\n**Decisions made** — Lazy GPU upload (textures uploaded on first render use, not at load time). Per-draw bind groups (not cached by material — future optimization). `GBufferPass::new` takes `\u0026Queue` for fallback texture creation.\n\n**Status** — Tested with Sketchfab GLB model, textures render correctly. Clippy clean, all tests pass."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:12:37.449864Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
